window.I9_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Steam Power & Engines 蒸汽動力與引擎","cards":[{"w":"steam engine","p":"n.","d":"a machine that uses steam to make power","c":"蒸汽機","s":"James Watt improved the steam engine in the 1760s, and factories soon used his design to run their machines.","t":"詹姆斯·瓦特在1760年代改良了蒸汽機,而工廠很快就用他的設計來運轉機器。"},{"w":"boiler","p":"n.","d":"a large container where water is heated into steam","c":"鍋爐","s":"The workers filled the boiler with water every morning, but they had to watch it carefully because it could explode.","t":"工人們每天早上把鍋爐裝滿水,但他們必須小心看著它,因為它可能會爆炸。"},{"w":"piston","p":"n.","d":"a part that moves up and down inside a tube in an engine","c":"活塞","s":"The steam pushed the piston up and down, and this movement turned the big wheel of the machine.","t":"蒸汽推動活塞上下移動,而這個動作帶動了機器的大輪子轉動。"},{"w":"cylinder","p":"n.","d":"a tube-shaped part of an engine where a piston moves","c":"汽缸","s":"Our science teacher showed us a model of an old engine, and we could see the piston moving inside the cylinder.","t":"我們的自然老師給我們看了一台舊引擎的模型,而我們可以看到活塞在汽缸裡移動。"},{"w":"valve","p":"n.","d":"a part that opens and closes to control gas or liquid","c":"閥門","s":"The engineer opened the valve slowly, so the extra steam could escape safely from the old engine.","t":"工程師慢慢打開閥門,好讓多餘的蒸汽能安全地從舊引擎中排出。"},{"w":"furnace","p":"n.","d":"a very hot enclosed fire used to heat or melt things","c":"熔爐;火爐","s":"The men shovelled coal into the furnace all day, and their faces were always black with dust.","t":"那些男人整天把煤鏟進熔爐裡,而他們的臉總是被灰塵弄得黑黑的。"},{"w":"flywheel","p":"n.","d":"a heavy wheel that keeps a machine turning smoothly","c":"飛輪","s":"The heavy flywheel kept spinning after the steam stopped, so the machine did not suddenly jerk to a halt.","t":"蒸汽停止後,沉重的飛輪仍持續轉動,所以機器不會突然猛地停下來。"},{"w":"crankshaft","p":"n.","d":"a rod in an engine that turns up-and-down movement into turning","c":"曲軸","s":"The mechanic said the crankshaft in my grandfather's old car was broken, and fixing it would cost a lot of money.","t":"技師說我祖父那輛舊車的曲軸壞了,而修理它要花很多錢。"},{"w":"horsepower","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring the power of an engine","c":"馬力","s":"Early cars had only a few horsepower, but people were still amazed because they did not need horses at all.","t":"早期的汽車只有幾匹馬力,但人們仍然很驚訝,因為它們完全不需要馬。"},{"w":"coal-fired","p":"adj.","d":"using coal as the fuel to produce heat or power","c":"燃煤的","s":"The town had a large coal-fired power station, and on windy days the smoke drifted over our school.","t":"這個鎮上有一座大型燃煤發電廠,而在颳風的日子,煙會飄到我們學校上空。"},{"w":"steam-powered","p":"adj.","d":"driven by the power of steam","c":"蒸汽動力的","s":"The museum still runs a steam-powered printing machine on weekends, and children love watching it work.","t":"博物館在週末仍會運轉一台蒸汽動力的印刷機,而孩子們很喜歡看它運作。"},{"w":"condenser","p":"n.","d":"a part that cools steam and turns it back into water","c":"冷凝器","s":"Watt added a separate condenser to the engine, so it wasted much less coal than older designs.","t":"瓦特在引擎上加了一個獨立的冷凝器,所以它比舊設計浪費的煤少得多。"},{"w":"chimney","p":"n.","d":"a tall pipe that carries smoke up and out of a building","c":"煙囪","s":"Hundreds of tall chimney rose above the city, and thick black smoke poured out of them day and night.","t":"數以百計高高的煙囪聳立在城市上方,而濃濃的黑煙日夜從裡面冒出來。"},{"w":"water wheel","p":"n.","d":"a large wheel turned by flowing water to power machines","c":"水車","s":"Before steam engines, many mills were built next to rivers because they needed a water wheel for power.","t":"在蒸汽機出現之前,許多磨坊都建在河邊,因為它們需要水車來提供動力。"},{"w":"windmill","p":"n.","d":"a building with sails that the wind turns to make power","c":"風車","s":"The old windmill on the hill once ground wheat into flour, but now it is a popular spot for photos.","t":"山丘上那座古老的風車曾經把小麥磨成麵粉,但現在它是熱門的拍照景點。"},{"w":"turbine","p":"n.","d":"a machine with blades that spin to produce power","c":"渦輪機","s":"Steam flows through the turbine at high speed, and the spinning blades help produce electricity for the city.","t":"蒸汽高速流過渦輪機,而旋轉的葉片幫助為城市產生電力。"},{"w":"dynamo","p":"n.","d":"a machine that turns movement into electricity","c":"發電機(直流)","s":"My bike has a small dynamo on the front wheel, so the light comes on when I pedal at night.","t":"我的腳踏車前輪上有一個小發電機,所以晚上我踩踏板時燈就會亮。"},{"w":"generator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that produces electricity","c":"發電機","s":"The power went off during the storm, but the hospital switched on its generator and kept working.","t":"暴風雨期間停電了,但醫院啟動了發電機並持續運作。"},{"w":"electricity","p":"n.","d":"a form of energy used for light, heat and machines","c":"電;電力","s":"Before electricity reached their village, families used oil lamps at night, and children did homework by candlelight.","t":"在電力到達他們的村莊之前,家家戶戶晚上用油燈,而孩子們在燭光下寫功課。"},{"w":"voltage","p":"n.","d":"the force of an electric current, measured in volts","c":"電壓","s":"You should check the voltage before you plug in your hair dryer abroad, or it may burn out.","t":"在國外插上吹風機之前你應該檢查電壓,否則它可能會燒壞。"},{"w":"vapour","p":"n.","d":"tiny drops of water or other liquid in the air","c":"蒸氣;水氣","s":"When the kettle boiled, white vapour rose into the cold kitchen, and the windows quickly became cloudy.","t":"水壺燒開時,白色的蒸氣升進寒冷的廚房,而窗戶很快就變得霧濛濛的。"},{"w":"internal combustion engine","p":"n.phr.","d":"an engine that burns fuel inside it to make power","c":"內燃機","s":"The internal combustion engine made cars lighter and faster, so steam cars slowly disappeared from the roads.","t":"內燃機讓汽車更輕更快,所以蒸汽車慢慢從道路上消失了。"},{"w":"spark plug","p":"n.","d":"a small part that makes a spark to light fuel in an engine","c":"火星塞","s":"My motorbike would not start this morning, and the mechanic said the spark plug needed to be replaced.","t":"我的機車今天早上發不動,而技師說火星塞需要更換。"},{"w":"overheat","p":"v.","d":"to become too hot","c":"過熱","s":"The old engine began to overheat on the steep hill, so we stopped and waited for it to cool down.","t":"那台舊引擎在陡坡上開始過熱,所以我們停下來等它冷卻。"},{"w":"lubricate","p":"v.","d":"to put oil on parts so they move smoothly","c":"潤滑;上油","s":"Workers had to lubricate the moving parts every day, because dry metal wore out very quickly.","t":"工人們每天都必須潤滑那些移動的零件,因為乾燥的金屬磨損得很快。"},{"w":"rust","p":"v.","d":"to become covered with a reddish layer when iron gets wet","c":"生鏽","s":"My dad left his tools outside in the rain, and after a week they began to rust badly.","t":"我爸把他的工具留在外面淋雨,而一週後它們開始嚴重生鏽。"},{"w":"pump","p":"n.","d":"a machine that pushes liquid or air in or out","c":"幫浦;抽水機","s":"Water kept flooding the mine, so the owners bought a steam pump to remove it day and night.","t":"水不斷淹進礦坑,所以礦主買了一台蒸汽抽水機日夜把水抽出。"},{"w":"stoke","p":"v.","d":"to add fuel to a fire and keep it burning strongly","c":"添加燃料;撥旺(火)","s":"On the old steam train, one man had to stoke the fire all the time, while the driver watched the track.","t":"在那列老蒸汽火車上,一個人必須一直添煤撥火,而司機則盯著鐵軌。"},{"w":"power station","p":"n.","d":"a place where electricity is produced","c":"發電廠","s":"The new power station supplies electricity to the whole county, but some residents worry about the noise.","t":"新的發電廠供電給整個郡,但一些居民擔心噪音問題。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Factories, Mills & Textiles 工廠、磨坊與紡織","cards":[{"w":"factory","p":"n.","d":"a building where goods are made in large numbers by machines","c":"工廠","s":"My aunt works in a shoe factory near the harbour, and she often has to work late before the holidays.","t":"我阿姨在港口附近的一家鞋子工廠工作,而假期前她經常得加班。"},{"w":"mill","p":"n.","d":"a building with machines for making cloth or flour","c":"磨坊;紡織廠","s":"The cotton mill employed over a thousand people, but the noise of the machines was almost unbearable.","t":"那家棉紡廠雇用了一千多人,但機器的噪音幾乎令人無法忍受。"},{"w":"cotton","p":"n.","d":"a soft white plant fibre used to make cloth","c":"棉花;棉","s":"Britain imported huge amounts of raw cotton, and its factories turned it into cheap cloth for the world.","t":"英國進口了大量的原棉,而它的工廠把棉花製成便宜的布料賣到全世界。"},{"w":"wool","p":"n.","d":"the soft hair of sheep, used to make cloth","c":"羊毛","s":"My grandmother knitted me a scarf from thick wool, and it keeps me warm on cold winter mornings.","t":"我奶奶用厚厚的羊毛為我織了一條圍巾,而它讓我在寒冷的冬天早晨保持溫暖。"},{"w":"spinning wheel","p":"n.","d":"a simple machine for making thread at home","c":"紡車","s":"Before factories, women made thread at home on a spinning wheel, but it took many hours to make enough.","t":"在工廠出現之前,婦女們在家用紡車紡線,但要花好幾個小時才能做出足夠的線。"},{"w":"spinning jenny","p":"n.","d":"an early machine that spun many threads at once","c":"珍妮紡紗機","s":"The spinning jenny could spin eight threads at once, so one worker could do the job of eight people.","t":"珍妮紡紗機一次可以紡八條線,所以一個工人就能做八個人的工作。"},{"w":"power loom","p":"n.","d":"a machine driven by power for weaving cloth","c":"動力織布機","s":"The power loom wove cloth much faster than hand weavers, and many of them lost their jobs.","t":"動力織布機織布比手工織工快得多,而他們之中許多人因此失業。"},{"w":"yarn","p":"n.","d":"long thread used for knitting or weaving","c":"紗線;毛線","s":"She bought some bright red yarn at the market, and she plans to knit a hat for her little brother.","t":"她在市場買了一些鮮紅色的毛線,而她打算為弟弟織一頂帽子。"},{"w":"thread","p":"n.","d":"a long thin string of cotton or other material used for sewing","c":"線","s":"The button on my coat fell off, so my mother sewed it back on with some black thread.","t":"我外套上的鈕扣掉了,所以我媽媽用一些黑色的線把它縫回去。"},{"w":"spindle","p":"n.","d":"a thin rod on which thread is wound when it is spun","c":"紡錘;錠子","s":"Each machine had hundreds of spindle turning at once, and children had to fix the broken threads quickly.","t":"每台機器上有數百個錠子同時轉動,而孩子們必須迅速接好斷掉的線。"},{"w":"cloth","p":"n.","d":"material made by weaving cotton, wool or other fibres","c":"布;布料","s":"The tailor measured me carefully, and then he cut the dark blue cloth to make my school uniform.","t":"裁縫仔細幫我量尺寸,然後他剪裁深藍色的布料來做我的校服。"},{"w":"garment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing","c":"衣服;服裝","s":"Every garment in this shop is made from recycled material, but the prices are still quite reasonable.","t":"這家店的每一件衣服都是用回收材料做的,但價格仍相當合理。"},{"w":"sewing machine","p":"n.","d":"a machine for joining cloth with thread","c":"縫紉機","s":"My mum bought an old sewing machine online, and now she makes curtains and bags for the whole family.","t":"我媽媽在網路上買了一台舊縫紉機,而現在她為全家人做窗簾和袋子。"},{"w":"weaver","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes cloth by crossing threads on a loom","c":"織工;織布工","s":"The village weaver worked at home for centuries, but factory machines soon took away their income.","t":"村裡的織工幾世紀以來都在家工作,但工廠的機器很快就奪走了他們的收入。"},{"w":"cottage industry","p":"n.phr.","d":"work done by people in their own homes","c":"家庭手工業","s":"Making lace was once a cottage industry in this area, and many families earned extra money from it.","t":"製作蕾絲曾經是這個地區的家庭手工業,而許多家庭藉此賺取額外收入。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where things are made or repaired","c":"工作坊;作坊","s":"Grandpa spends every afternoon in his workshop, and he has built three wooden chairs this year.","t":"爺爺每天下午都待在他的工作坊裡,而他今年已經做了三張木椅。"},{"w":"foreman","p":"n.","d":"a worker who is in charge of a group of other workers","c":"工頭;領班","s":"The foreman shouted at the boys to work faster, but they were too tired after twelve hours.","t":"工頭對著男孩們大吼要他們做快一點,但工作十二小時後他們已經太累了。"},{"w":"mechanise","p":"v.","d":"to start using machines to do work","c":"使機械化","s":"Farmers began to mechanise their work in the 1800s, so fewer people were needed in the fields.","t":"農民在1800年代開始讓工作機械化,所以田裡需要的人手變少了。"},{"w":"mechanisation","p":"n.","d":"the use of machines to replace human or animal work","c":"機械化","s":"mechanisation made cloth much cheaper, but it also caused many skilled workers to lose their jobs.","t":"機械化讓布料便宜很多,但也導致許多熟練工人失去工作。"},{"w":"mill owner","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns a factory or mill","c":"工廠主;磨坊主","s":"The rich mill owner built houses for his workers, while other owners did not care where workers lived.","t":"那位富有的工廠主為他的工人蓋了房子,而其他工廠主並不在乎工人住在哪裡。"},{"w":"raw material","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance used to make products","c":"原料","s":"Cotton was the main raw material for the mills, so ships brought it across the ocean every week.","t":"棉花是工廠的主要原料,所以船隻每週都把它運過大洋。"},{"w":"finished goods","p":"n.","d":"products that are ready to be sold","c":"成品","s":"The factory turned cotton into finished goods, and trains carried them to shops all over the country.","t":"工廠把棉花變成成品,而火車把它們運到全國各地的商店。"},{"w":"manufacturer","p":"n.","d":"a company that makes goods in large amounts","c":"製造商","s":"This toy manufacturer moved its factory to another country, because the costs there were much lower.","t":"這家玩具製造商把工廠遷到另一個國家,因為那裡的成本低得多。"},{"w":"workbench","p":"n.","d":"a strong table used for making or repairing things","c":"工作檯","s":"He laid all the clock parts on the workbench, and he slowly put them back together one by one.","t":"他把所有的時鐘零件攤在工作檯上,然後慢慢地一個一個把它們組裝回去。"},{"w":"artisan","p":"n.","d":"a skilled person who makes things by hand","c":"工匠;手藝人","s":"This market sells bread from a local artisan, and people queue early because it sells out fast.","t":"這個市場販售當地一位手藝人做的麵包,而人們很早就排隊,因為很快就賣光了。"},{"w":"handmade","p":"adj.","d":"made by hand, not by machine","c":"手工製作的","s":"Her handmade pottery is more expensive than factory cups, but every piece has its own special pattern.","t":"她手工製作的陶器比工廠做的杯子貴,但每一件都有自己獨特的圖案。"},{"w":"machine-made","p":"adj.","d":"produced by a machine, not by hand","c":"機器製造的","s":"machine-made socks were much cheaper than knitted ones, so poor families could finally afford new clothes.","t":"機器製造的襪子比手織的便宜很多,所以貧窮的家庭終於買得起新衣服。"},{"w":"cotton gin","p":"n.","d":"a machine that separates cotton fibres from seeds","c":"軋棉機","s":"The cotton gin cleaned cotton very quickly, but sadly it also increased the demand for slave labour.","t":"軋棉機能很快地清理棉花,但可悲的是它也增加了對奴隸勞動的需求。"},{"w":"interchangeable parts","p":"n.phr.","d":"identical parts that can replace each other easily","c":"可互換零件","s":"Guns made with interchangeable parts were easy to repair, because a broken piece could simply be swapped.","t":"用可互換零件製造的槍很容易修理,因為壞掉的零件只要直接換掉就好。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Mining, Iron & Steel 採礦與鋼鐵","cards":[{"w":"coal mine","p":"n.","d":"a place underground where coal is dug out","c":"煤礦","s":"My great-grandfather worked in a coal mine when he was only twelve, and he rarely saw the sun in winter.","t":"我曾祖父十二歲時就在煤礦工作,而他在冬天很少見到太陽。"},{"w":"colliery","p":"n.","d":"a coal mine and the buildings around it","c":"煤礦場","s":"The colliery closed in 1985, and many families in the valley had to move away to find work.","t":"那座煤礦場在1985年關閉了,而山谷裡的許多家庭必須搬走去找工作。"},{"w":"miner","p":"n.","d":"a person who works under the ground digging coal or metal","c":"礦工","s":"The miner went down into the dark tunnels every morning, and their families waited nervously for them.","t":"礦工們每天早上下到黑暗的坑道裡,而他們的家人緊張地等著他們回來。"},{"w":"mine shaft","p":"n.","d":"a deep hole going down into a mine","c":"礦井","s":"The workers rode a small lift down the mine shaft, and the air grew hotter as they went deeper.","t":"工人們乘坐小升降機沿著礦井下去,而越往深處空氣就越熱。"},{"w":"tunnel","p":"n.","d":"a long passage under the ground","c":"隧道;坑道","s":"The train went into a long tunnel under the mountain, and suddenly my phone lost its signal.","t":"火車開進山底下一條長長的隧道,而我的手機突然沒有訊號了。"},{"w":"ore","p":"n.","d":"rock from which metal can be taken","c":"礦石","s":"The rocks in this area contain copper ore, so a mining company wants to start digging here.","t":"這個地區的岩石含有銅礦石,所以一家礦業公司想在這裡開挖。"},{"w":"iron ore","p":"n.","d":"rock that contains iron","c":"鐵礦石","s":"Australia exports a lot of iron ore to Asia, and much of it is turned into steel for buildings.","t":"澳洲出口大量鐵礦石到亞洲,而其中很多被製成建築用的鋼材。"},{"w":"cast iron","p":"n.","d":"hard iron that is shaped by pouring it into a mould","c":"鑄鐵","s":"My mother cooks with a heavy cast iron pan, and she says it lasts much longer than modern ones.","t":"我媽媽用一個沉重的鑄鐵鍋煮飯,而她說它比現代的鍋子耐用得多。"},{"w":"wrought iron","p":"n.","d":"iron that is heated and bent into shapes by hand","c":"鍛鐵;熟鐵","s":"The old park has beautiful wrought iron gates, and tourists often stop to take pictures of them.","t":"那座老公園有漂亮的鍛鐵大門,而遊客經常停下來拍照。"},{"w":"pig iron","p":"n.","d":"rough iron that comes straight from a furnace","c":"生鐵","s":"Workers poured the hot pig iron into sand moulds, and then it was sent away to be made into steel.","t":"工人們把熾熱的生鐵倒進沙模中,然後它被送去製成鋼。"},{"w":"blast furnace","p":"n.","d":"a huge furnace where hot air helps melt iron from rock","c":"高爐;鼓風爐","s":"The blast furnace burned day and night, so the sky above the town glowed orange after dark.","t":"那座高爐日夜燃燒,所以天黑後鎮上的天空都閃著橘色的光。"},{"w":"ironworks","p":"n.","d":"a factory where iron is made","c":"鐵工廠;煉鐵廠","s":"The town grew quickly around the ironworks, and its population doubled in only twenty years.","t":"這個小鎮圍繞著煉鐵廠迅速發展,而它的人口在短短二十年間就翻倍了。"},{"w":"steelworks","p":"n.","d":"a factory where steel is made","c":"鋼鐵廠","s":"My uncle got a job at the steelworks after school, and he worked there for over thirty years.","t":"我舅舅畢業後在鋼鐵廠找到工作,而他在那裡工作了三十多年。"},{"w":"foundry","p":"n.","d":"a factory where metal is melted and shaped","c":"鑄造廠","s":"The bells for the church were made at a local foundry, and each one weighed more than a car.","t":"教堂的鐘是在當地一家鑄造廠製作的,而每一個都比一輛車還重。"},{"w":"molten","p":"adj.","d":"melted by very great heat","c":"熔化的","s":"The workers wore thick gloves while they poured the molten metal, because one drop could burn through skin.","t":"工人們倒熔化的金屬時戴著厚手套,因為一滴就能燙穿皮膚。"},{"w":"mould","p":"n.","d":"a hollow shape into which hot liquid is poured","c":"模具;鑄模","s":"We poured melted chocolate into a heart-shaped mould, and then we put it in the fridge to set.","t":"我們把融化的巧克力倒進心形的模具裡,然後把它放進冰箱定型。"},{"w":"anvil","p":"n.","d":"a heavy iron block on which hot metal is hammered","c":"鐵砧","s":"The smith hammered the red-hot metal on the anvil, and sparks flew across the dark room.","t":"鐵匠在鐵砧上敲打燒紅的金屬,而火花在昏暗的房間裡四處飛濺。"},{"w":"blacksmith","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes things from iron by heating and hammering","c":"鐵匠","s":"Every village once had a blacksmith who made horseshoes, but few people learn this skill today.","t":"以前每個村莊都有一位做馬蹄鐵的鐵匠,但現在很少人學這項技藝了。"},{"w":"steel","p":"n.","d":"a strong metal made from iron and carbon","c":"鋼","s":"Modern skyscrapers have frames made of steel, so they can be much taller than old stone buildings.","t":"現代摩天大樓的骨架是用鋼做的,所以它們可以比古老的石造建築高得多。"},{"w":"Bessemer process","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cheap way to make steel by blowing air through iron","c":"貝塞麥煉鋼法","s":"The Bessemer process made steel cheap for the first time, so railways and bridges could use it everywhere.","t":"貝塞麥煉鋼法首次讓鋼變得便宜,所以鐵路和橋梁各處都能使用它。"},{"w":"impurity","p":"n.","d":"an unwanted substance mixed into something","c":"雜質","s":"Blowing air through the hot iron burned away each impurity, and the metal became much stronger.","t":"讓空氣吹過熾熱的鐵會燒掉每一種雜質,而金屬變得堅固許多。"},{"w":"coal seam","p":"n.","d":"a layer of coal under the ground","c":"煤層","s":"The miners found a thick coal seam deep underground, but reaching it safely was very difficult.","t":"礦工們在地底深處發現一個厚厚的煤層,但要安全地挖到它非常困難。"},{"w":"pickaxe","p":"n.","d":"a heavy tool with a pointed metal head for breaking rock","c":"鶴嘴鋤;十字鎬","s":"Each miner carried a pickaxe and a lamp, and they broke the hard rock by hand for hours.","t":"每位礦工都帶著一把十字鎬和一盞燈,而他們徒手敲碎堅硬的岩石好幾個小時。"},{"w":"explosion","p":"n.","d":"a sudden violent burst with a loud noise","c":"爆炸","s":"Gas in the mine caused a terrible explosion, and the whole town gathered at the gate for news.","t":"礦坑裡的瓦斯引發了一場可怕的爆炸,而全鎮的人都聚集在大門口等消息。"},{"w":"safety lamp","p":"n.","d":"a special lamp that will not light gas in a mine","c":"安全燈","s":"The new safety lamp protected miners from deadly gas explosions, so far fewer men died underground after 1816.","t":"新的安全燈保護礦工免於致命的瓦斯爆炸,所以1816年後在地下喪生的人少了很多。"},{"w":"metallurgy","p":"n.","d":"the science of metals and how to use them","c":"冶金學","s":"My cousin studies metallurgy at university, and she hopes to design lighter metals for planes one day.","t":"我表姊在大學唸冶金學,而她希望有一天能為飛機設計更輕的金屬。"},{"w":"rivet","p":"n.","d":"a short metal pin used to join metal sheets together","c":"鉚釘","s":"The Eiffel Tower is held together by millions of rivet, and workers put each one in by hand.","t":"艾菲爾鐵塔是由數百萬顆鉚釘固定起來的,而工人們是一顆一顆用手裝上去的。"},{"w":"girder","p":"n.","d":"a long strong metal beam that supports a building or bridge","c":"大樑;鋼樑","s":"A crane lifted the huge steel girder into place, while workers on the bridge guided it carefully.","t":"起重機把巨大的鋼樑吊到定位,而橋上的工人小心地引導它。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Transport: Railways, Canals & Cars 交通運輸:鐵路、運河與汽車","cards":[{"w":"railway","p":"n.","d":"a system of tracks and trains for moving people and goods","c":"鐵路","s":"The first public railway opened in 1825, and soon people could travel between cities in hours, not days.","t":"第一條公共鐵路在1825年開通,而很快人們就能在幾小時內而非幾天內往返城市。"},{"w":"locomotive","p":"n.","d":"the engine that pulls a train","c":"火車頭;機車","s":"The old steam locomotive is kept in the museum, and visitors can climb into the driver's cab.","t":"那輛老蒸汽火車頭保存在博物館裡,而參觀者可以爬進司機室。"},{"w":"steam train","p":"n.","d":"a train pulled by an engine that uses steam","c":"蒸汽火車","s":"We rode an old steam train through the mountains, and the whistle echoed loudly across the valley.","t":"我們搭乘一列老蒸汽火車穿越山區,而汽笛聲在山谷間響亮地迴盪。"},{"w":"railway track","p":"n.","d":"the metal rails that trains run on","c":"鐵軌","s":"Never walk along the railway track, because trains move faster than you think and cannot stop quickly.","t":"絕對不要沿著鐵軌走,因為火車行駛得比你想的快,而且無法很快停下來。"},{"w":"rail","p":"n.","d":"a train system; travel by train","c":"鐵路(運輸)","s":"Travelling by rail is better for the environment, so our school took the train to the science museum.","t":"搭鐵路旅行對環境比較好,所以我們學校搭火車去科學博物館。"},{"w":"carriage","p":"n.","d":"one of the separate parts of a train where people sit","c":"(火車)車廂","s":"The front carriage was very crowded, so we walked to the back of the train and found empty seats.","t":"前面的車廂非常擠,所以我們走到火車後段並找到了空位。"},{"w":"wagon","p":"n.","d":"a part of a train for carrying goods","c":"貨車車廂","s":"Each wagon was filled with coal, and the long train moved slowly towards the port.","t":"每一節貨車車廂都裝滿了煤,而那列長長的火車緩緩駛向港口。"},{"w":"station","p":"n.","d":"a place where trains stop for passengers","c":"車站","s":"We arrived at the station ten minutes early, but the train was delayed because of heavy snow.","t":"我們提早十分鐘到達車站,但火車因為大雪而誤點了。"},{"w":"level crossing","p":"n.","d":"a place where a road crosses a railway line","c":"平交道","s":"The barriers came down at the level crossing, so all the cars waited while the train rushed past.","t":"平交道的柵欄放下來了,所以所有車子都在等待,而火車呼嘯而過。"},{"w":"passenger","p":"n.","d":"a person travelling in a vehicle who is not driving","c":"乘客","s":"Every passenger must wear a seat belt on this bus, and the driver will not leave until everyone does.","t":"這輛公車上每位乘客都必須繫安全帶,而司機在所有人繫好前不會開車。"},{"w":"canal","p":"n.","d":"a man-made river for boats","c":"運河","s":"Before railways, factories sent goods along the canal, because boats could carry heavy loads cheaply.","t":"在鐵路出現之前,工廠沿著運河運送貨物,因為船隻能便宜地載運重物。"},{"w":"lock","p":"n.","d":"a section of a canal with gates to raise or lower boats","c":"(運河)水閘;船閘","s":"Our boat entered the lock, and the water slowly rose until we could continue up the hill.","t":"我們的船駛進船閘,而水慢慢上升,直到我們能繼續往山上航行。"},{"w":"barge","p":"n.","d":"a long flat boat for carrying goods on rivers or canals","c":"駁船","s":"A horse pulled the heavy barge along the canal, and a boy walked beside it with a stick.","t":"一匹馬沿著運河拉著沉重的駁船,而一個男孩拿著棍子走在牠旁邊。"},{"w":"towpath","p":"n.","d":"a path beside a canal where horses once pulled boats","c":"(運河邊的)縴道","s":"Today people cycle along the old towpath, but in the past it was used by horses pulling boats.","t":"現在人們沿著舊縴道騎腳踏車,但在過去它是給拉船的馬使用的。"},{"w":"steamship","p":"n.","d":"a large ship driven by steam power","c":"蒸汽船;輪船","s":"The steamship crossed the Atlantic in two weeks, so letters and goods arrived much sooner than before.","t":"那艘蒸汽船兩週就橫越大西洋,所以信件和貨物比以前早得多送達。"},{"w":"paddle steamer","p":"n.","d":"a steamboat moved by large turning wheels on its sides","c":"明輪汽船","s":"We took a trip on an old paddle steamer, and the big wheels splashed loudly as we moved down the river.","t":"我們搭乘一艘老明輪汽船遊覽,而當我們順河而下時,大輪子嘩啦嘩啦地拍打著水。"},{"w":"horse-drawn","p":"adj.","d":"pulled by a horse","c":"馬拉的","s":"horse-drawn carts were common in big cities, but they made the streets dirty, noisy and very slow.","t":"馬拉的貨車在大城市很常見,但它們讓街道變得又髒、又吵、又非常緩慢。"},{"w":"automobile","p":"n.","d":"a car","c":"汽車","s":"Karl Benz built the first practical automobile in 1885, and within fifty years cars had changed city life.","t":"卡爾·賓士在1885年製造出第一輛實用的汽車,而在五十年內汽車就改變了城市生活。"},{"w":"motor car","p":"n.","d":"an old-fashioned word for a car","c":"汽車(舊稱)","s":"My great-grandmother remembered the first motor car in her village, and everyone ran outside to look at it.","t":"我曾祖母記得她村裡的第一輛汽車,而大家都跑出去看它。"},{"w":"steam car","p":"n.","d":"a car that uses a steam engine","c":"蒸汽汽車","s":"The steam car was quiet and powerful, but it took too long to start on cold mornings.","t":"蒸汽汽車安靜又有力,但在寒冷的早晨要花太久時間才能啟動。"},{"w":"bicycle","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle with two wheels that you ride by pushing pedals","c":"腳踏車","s":"The bicycle gave working people cheap freedom, so they could visit the countryside on weekends.","t":"腳踏車給了勞工們便宜的自由,讓他們週末可以去鄉間遊玩。"},{"w":"tyre","p":"n.","d":"a rubber ring filled with air around a wheel","c":"輪胎","s":"I got a flat tyre on the way to school, so I had to push my bike for the last two kilometres.","t":"我在上學途中輪胎爆了,所以最後兩公里我只好牽著腳踏車走。"},{"w":"chassis","p":"n.","d":"the frame of a vehicle that holds the engine and body","c":"底盤;車架","s":"The factory first builds the chassis, and then workers add the engine, wheels and seats.","t":"工廠先打造底盤,然後工人們加上引擎、輪子和座椅。"},{"w":"steering wheel","p":"n.","d":"the wheel a driver turns to control a car's direction","c":"方向盤","s":"Early cars used a stick instead of a steering wheel, so turning corners was quite difficult.","t":"早期汽車用一根桿子而不是方向盤,所以轉彎相當困難。"},{"w":"brake","p":"n.","d":"a part that makes a vehicle slow down or stop","c":"煞車","s":"The driver hit the brake when a dog ran into the road, and luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"一隻狗衝到馬路上時司機踩了煞車,而幸好沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"engine driver","p":"n.","d":"a person who drives a train","c":"火車司機","s":"The engine driver blew the whistle twice, and the children on the platform waved goodbye.","t":"火車司機鳴了兩次汽笛,而月台上的孩子們揮手道別。"},{"w":"conductor","p":"n.","d":"a person who checks tickets on a train or bus","c":"車掌;列車長","s":"The conductor checked our tickets carefully, but he let my little brother travel for free.","t":"車掌仔細檢查我們的車票,但他讓我弟弟免費搭乘。"},{"w":"viaduct","p":"n.","d":"a long high bridge that carries a road or railway across a valley","c":"高架橋","s":"The train crossed a tall stone viaduct, and we could see the river far below our window.","t":"火車越過一座高高的石造高架橋,而我們從窗戶可以看到遠在下方的河流。"},{"w":"commuter","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels some distance to work every day","c":"通勤者","s":"My father is a daily commuter who takes the 7:15 train into the city, and he reads the news on his phone during the trip.","t":"我爸爸是每天搭7點15分火車進城的通勤者,而他在車程中用手機看新聞。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Inventors, Inventions & Science 發明家、發明與科學","cards":[{"w":"inventor","p":"n.","d":"a person who creates something new for the first time","c":"發明家","s":"Thomas Edison was a famous inventor, but he worked with a large team of skilled assistants.","t":"湯瑪斯·愛迪生是一位著名的發明家,但他和一大群熟練的助手一起工作。"},{"w":"invention","p":"n.","d":"something new that someone has made or designed","c":"發明;發明物","s":"The printing press was an important invention, because it let ideas spread quickly across Europe.","t":"印刷機是一項重要的發明,因為它讓思想迅速在歐洲傳播。"},{"w":"invent","p":"v.","d":"to make or design something that did not exist before","c":"發明","s":"Alexander Graham Bell invent the telephone in 1876, and soon people could talk across long distances.","t":"亞歷山大·格拉漢姆·貝爾在1876年發明了電話,而很快人們就能遠距離交談。"},{"w":"ingenious","p":"adj.","d":"very clever and original","c":"巧妙的;有創意的","s":"My brother found an ingenious way to water his plants while we were away, and none of them died.","t":"我哥哥想到一個巧妙的方法在我們外出時幫植物澆水,而沒有一株枯死。"},{"w":"tinker","p":"v.","d":"to try to repair or improve something by small changes","c":"修補;擺弄","s":"He loves to tinker with old radios in the garage, and sometimes he makes them work again.","t":"他喜歡在車庫裡擺弄舊收音機,而有時候他能讓它們重新運作。"},{"w":"trial","p":"n.","d":"a test to see if something works well","c":"試驗;試用","s":"The new engine failed its first trial, but the engineers fixed the problem within a week.","t":"新引擎第一次試驗失敗了,但工程師們在一週內就解決了問題。"},{"w":"experiment","p":"n.","d":"a scientific test to find out something","c":"實驗","s":"We did a simple experiment in class with magnets, and everyone was surprised by the results.","t":"我們在課堂上用磁鐵做了一個簡單的實驗,而大家都對結果感到驚訝。"},{"w":"mechanic","p":"n.","d":"a person who repairs engines and machines","c":"技師;修車工","s":"The mechanic found the problem quickly, but he needed two days to order the right part.","t":"技師很快就找到了問題,但他需要兩天來訂購正確的零件。"},{"w":"engineering","p":"n.","d":"the work of designing and building machines, roads and bridges","c":"工程(學)","s":"She wants to study engineering at university, because she loves solving problems and building things.","t":"她想在大學唸工程,因為她熱愛解決問題和動手做東西。"},{"w":"physicist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies energy, force and matter","c":"物理學家","s":"The physicist explained how electricity works, and the audience finally understood why lights switch on.","t":"那位物理學家解釋了電是怎麼運作的,而觀眾終於明白燈為什麼會亮。"},{"w":"chemist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies substances and how they change","c":"化學家","s":"A young chemist discovered the first artificial dye by accident, and it made him very rich.","t":"一位年輕的化學家意外發現了第一種人工染料,而它讓他變得非常富有。"},{"w":"discovery","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding something that was not known before","c":"發現","s":"The discovery of electricity changed everyday life, but it took many years to reach ordinary homes.","t":"電的發現改變了日常生活,但它花了很多年才進入一般家庭。"},{"w":"innovator","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces new ideas or methods","c":"創新者","s":"Steve Jobs is often called an innovator, although many people helped him create his famous products.","t":"史蒂夫·賈伯斯常被稱為創新者,雖然有很多人幫他打造出那些知名產品。"},{"w":"improvement","p":"n.","d":"a change that makes something better","c":"改進;改善","s":"Watt's improvement to the steam engine saved coal, so factory owners were eager to buy his machines.","t":"瓦特對蒸汽機的改進節省了煤,所以工廠老闆們都急著買他的機器。"},{"w":"contraption","p":"n.","d":"a strange or complicated machine or device","c":"奇怪的裝置","s":"My little sister built a funny contraption from boxes and string, and it actually feeds the cat.","t":"我妹妹用箱子和繩子做了一個好笑的奇怪裝置,而它居然真的能餵貓。"},{"w":"gizmo","p":"n.","d":"a small clever device (informal)","c":"小玩意兒;小裝置","s":"Dad bought a new kitchen gizmo that peels apples, but we still prefer using a knife.","t":"爸爸買了一個能削蘋果皮的新廚房小玩意兒,但我們還是比較喜歡用刀子。"},{"w":"imitation","p":"n.","d":"a copy of something","c":"仿製品;模仿","s":"The shop sold a cheap imitation of the famous watch, but it stopped working after a month.","t":"那家店賣那款名錶的便宜仿製品,但它一個月後就壞了。"},{"w":"royalty","p":"n.","d":"money paid to an inventor or writer each time their work is used","c":"權利金;版稅","s":"The inventor received a royalty for every machine sold, so he earned money for many years.","t":"發明家每賣出一台機器就收到一筆權利金,所以他好多年都持續有收入。"},{"w":"trademark","p":"n.","d":"a name or sign that belongs to one company","c":"商標","s":"The company protected its trademark carefully, because the name was famous all over the world.","t":"那家公司小心保護它的商標,因為那個名稱聞名全世界。"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that gives money to support something","c":"贊助者;贊助商","s":"The young inventor found a rich sponsor, so he could finally build a full-size model of his machine.","t":"那位年輕發明家找到一位富有的贊助者,所以他終於能打造機器的實物大小模型。"},{"w":"backer","p":"n.","d":"someone who supports a project with money","c":"資助者;支持者","s":"The project failed when its main backer pulled out, and the workshop had to close.","t":"當主要資助者撤資時那個計畫就失敗了,而工作坊也不得不關門。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public show of objects or works","c":"展覽","s":"The Great exhibition of 1851 showed amazing new machines, and six million people came to see them.","t":"1851年的萬國博覽會展出了驚人的新機器,而有六百萬人前來參觀。"},{"w":"demonstration","p":"n.","d":"showing how something works","c":"示範;展示","s":"The inventor gave a demonstration of his new telephone, and the crowd cheered when they heard his voice.","t":"發明家為他的新電話做了一場示範,而當群眾聽到他的聲音時都歡呼起來。"},{"w":"world's fair","p":"n.","d":"a large international exhibition of new products and ideas","c":"世界博覽會","s":"The Eiffel Tower was built for a world's fair in 1889, but it later became a symbol of Paris.","t":"艾菲爾鐵塔是為1889年的世界博覽會而建造的,但後來它成為了巴黎的象徵。"},{"w":"inventive","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ideas","c":"有創造力的","s":"Our science teacher is very inventive, and she often turns rubbish into tools for our experiments.","t":"我們的自然老師非常有創造力,而她常把垃圾變成我們做實驗的工具。"},{"w":"sketch","p":"n.","d":"a quick simple drawing","c":"草圖;素描","s":"Leonardo da Vinci made a sketch of a flying machine, but nobody could build it at that time.","t":"李奧納多·達文西畫了一張飛行機器的草圖,但當時沒有人能把它造出來。"},{"w":"magnet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of metal that pulls iron towards it","c":"磁鐵","s":"I keep my shopping list on the fridge with a magnet, so I never forget it when I go out.","t":"我用磁鐵把購物清單貼在冰箱上,所以我出門時從不會忘記。"},{"w":"magnetism","p":"n.","d":"the force that magnets produce","c":"磁性;磁力","s":"Scientists studied magnetism and electricity together in the 1820s, and their work led to the first electric motors.","t":"科學家們在1820年代一起研究磁力和電,而他們的成果催生了第一批電動馬達。"},{"w":"wire","p":"n.","d":"a long thin piece of metal used to carry electricity","c":"電線;金屬線","s":"The lamp stopped working because a wire was loose, so my dad fixed it with a screwdriver.","t":"這盞燈不亮了是因為一條電線鬆了,所以我爸用螺絲起子修好了它。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Social Change: Workers, Cities & Reform 社會變遷:勞工、城市與改革","cards":[{"w":"industrialisation","p":"n.","d":"the growth of factories and industry in a country","c":"工業化","s":"industrialisation brought many new jobs to the cities, but it also brought pollution and crowded housing.","t":"工業化為城市帶來了許多新的工作機會,但也帶來了污染和擁擠的住屋。"},{"w":"working class","p":"n.","d":"people who do physical or factory work for wages","c":"勞工階級","s":"The working class worked long hours in the mills, while the owners lived in large houses outside town.","t":"勞工階級在工廠裡長時間工作,而工廠老闆則住在鎮外的大房子裡。"},{"w":"middle class","p":"n.","d":"people with average income, such as teachers and shopkeepers","c":"中產階級","s":"The middle class grew quickly in the 1800s, and these families could afford pianos and books.","t":"中產階級在1800年代迅速成長,而這些家庭買得起鋼琴和書籍。"},{"w":"factory worker","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a factory","c":"工廠工人","s":"As a factory worker, my grandmother sewed shirts all day, but she still found time to read at night.","t":"身為工廠工人,我祖母整天縫襯衫,但她晚上仍會抽空閱讀。"},{"w":"child labour","p":"n.","d":"the use of children as workers","c":"童工","s":"child labour was common in early factories, because children were small and their wages were low.","t":"童工在早期工廠很常見,因為孩子們個子小而且工資低。"},{"w":"working conditions","p":"n.","d":"the hours, safety and environment of a job","c":"工作環境;勞動條件","s":"The workers went on strike because their working conditions were dangerous, and the owners refused to listen.","t":"工人們罷工是因為他們的工作環境很危險,而老闆們拒絕傾聽。"},{"w":"slum","p":"n.","d":"a very poor, crowded and dirty area of a city","c":"貧民窟","s":"Thousands of families lived in the slum near the factories, and diseases spread quickly there.","t":"數千個家庭住在工廠附近的貧民窟裡,而疾病在那裡迅速傳播。"},{"w":"tenement","p":"n.","d":"a large old building divided into small flats for poor families","c":"廉價公寓;出租公寓","s":"Eight people shared one room in the tenement, and they used a single toilet with the whole building.","t":"八個人擠在廉價公寓的一個房間裡,而他們和整棟樓的人共用一間廁所。"},{"w":"overcrowded","p":"adj.","d":"having too many people in a space","c":"過度擁擠的","s":"The trains are overcrowded during rush hour, so I usually leave home early to get a seat.","t":"尖峰時段火車過度擁擠,所以我通常提早出門好找到座位。"},{"w":"sanitation","p":"n.","d":"systems for clean water and removing waste","c":"衛生設施;公共衛生","s":"Better sanitation in the cities saved thousands of lives, because clean water stopped many deadly diseases from spreading.","t":"城市裡更好的衛生設施拯救了數千條人命,因為乾淨的水阻止了許多致命疾病的傳播。"},{"w":"cholera","p":"n.","d":"a serious disease caused by dirty water","c":"霍亂","s":"John Snow traced a cholera outbreak to one water pump, and the city removed its handle to stop it.","t":"約翰·斯諾把一場霍亂疫情追查到一座抽水機,而市政府拆掉它的把手來阻止疫情。"},{"w":"trade union","p":"n.","d":"an organisation of workers that protects their rights","c":"工會","s":"The workers formed a trade union, so they could ask for better pay together instead of alone.","t":"工人們組成了一個工會,這樣他們就能一起而非單獨爭取更好的薪水。"},{"w":"strike","p":"n.","d":"a time when workers stop working to protest","c":"罷工","s":"The bus drivers went on strike last week, so many students had to walk or cycle to school.","t":"公車司機上週舉行罷工,所以許多學生只好走路或騎腳踏車上學。"},{"w":"reformer","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to improve society","c":"改革者","s":"The reformer visited the dirty factories herself, and her reports shocked many people in the government.","t":"那位改革者親自走訪骯髒的工廠,而她的報告震驚了許多政府官員。"},{"w":"minimum wage","p":"n.","d":"the lowest pay that the law allows","c":"最低工資","s":"The government raised the minimum wage this year, but some shop owners say they cannot afford it.","t":"政府今年調高了最低工資,但一些店家老闆說他們負擔不起。"},{"w":"landlord","p":"n.","d":"a person who rents a house or room to others","c":"房東","s":"Our landlord raised the rent again, so my family is looking for a cheaper flat near my school.","t":"我們的房東又調漲房租了,所以我家正在我學校附近找比較便宜的公寓。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the countryside","c":"鄉村的;農村的","s":"Many young people left rural areas for the big cities, because factories offered steady work and pay.","t":"許多年輕人離開鄉村地區前往大城市,因為工廠提供穩定的工作和薪水。"},{"w":"population growth","p":"n.","d":"an increase in the number of people","c":"人口成長","s":"Fast population growth made the cities crowded, and the government struggled to build enough homes.","t":"快速的人口成長讓城市變得擁擠,而政府難以蓋足夠的房子。"},{"w":"workhouse","p":"n.","d":"a place where very poor people lived and worked in the past","c":"濟貧院;救濟院","s":"In Oliver Twist, the boy grows up in a workhouse, and he is punished for asking for more food.","t":"在《孤雛淚》中,那個男孩在濟貧院長大,而他因為要求多一點食物而受罰。"},{"w":"chimney sweep","p":"n.","d":"a person who cleans chimneys","c":"掃煙囪工人","s":"In the past, a small boy often worked as a chimney sweep, because he could climb inside narrow chimneys.","t":"過去,小男孩常常當掃煙囪工人,因為他能爬進狹窄的煙囪裡。"},{"w":"apprentice","p":"n.","d":"a young person learning a skill from an expert","c":"學徒","s":"He worked as an apprentice to a carpenter for four years, and now he runs his own furniture business.","t":"他當了四年木匠的學徒,而現在他經營自己的家具事業。"},{"w":"sweatshop","p":"n.","d":"a factory where people work long hours for very low pay","c":"血汗工廠","s":"Some cheap clothes are made in a sweatshop, so we should check where our clothes come from.","t":"有些便宜的衣服是在血汗工廠裡製造的,所以我們應該查查衣服的來源。"},{"w":"riot","p":"n.","d":"a violent protest by a crowd of people","c":"暴動","s":"Hungry workers started a riot when bread prices rose, and soldiers were sent to the town.","t":"當麵包價格上漲時,飢餓的工人們發起了暴動,而士兵被派往那個小鎮。"},{"w":"capitalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who uses money to own businesses and make profit","c":"資本家","s":"The capitalist invested in new machines, and he made huge profits while his workers stayed poor.","t":"那位資本家投資新機器,而他賺取了巨額利潤,他的工人卻仍然貧窮。"},{"w":"capitalism","p":"n.","d":"an economic system based on private business and profit","c":"資本主義","s":"Under capitalism, companies compete to sell products, so prices can fall but some people are left behind.","t":"在資本主義之下,公司們競爭銷售產品,所以價格可能下降,但有些人被拋在後頭。"},{"w":"consumer goods","p":"n.","d":"products that people buy for their own use","c":"消費品","s":"Factories made consumer goods like soap and shoes cheaper, so ordinary families could buy more.","t":"工廠讓肥皂和鞋子這類消費品變得更便宜,所以一般家庭能買得更多。"},{"w":"standard of living","p":"n.phr.","d":"how comfortable and wealthy people's lives are","c":"生活水準","s":"Their standard of living improved slowly, but it took decades before workers could afford good housing.","t":"他們的生活水準慢慢提升,但過了幾十年工人才負擔得起好的住屋。"},{"w":"life expectancy","p":"n.","d":"the average number of years a person is likely to live","c":"平均壽命;預期壽命","s":"life expectancy in factory towns was very low, but clean water and better food slowly raised it.","t":"工廠城鎮的平均壽命非常低,但乾淨的水和更好的食物慢慢地提高了它。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Communication & Everyday Inventions 通訊與日常發明","cards":[{"w":"telegraph","p":"n.","d":"an old system for sending messages along wires using signals","c":"電報","s":"News of the battle came by telegraph, so people in London knew about it on the same day.","t":"戰役的消息透過電報傳來,所以倫敦的人們在同一天就知道了。"},{"w":"Morse code","p":"n.","d":"a code of short and long signals for letters","c":"摩斯密碼","s":"The soldiers sent short messages in Morse code, and only trained operators could understand them quickly.","t":"士兵們用摩斯密碼傳送簡短訊息,而只有受過訓練的操作員能迅速看懂。"},{"w":"telephone","p":"n.","d":"a device for talking to someone far away","c":"電話","s":"My grandparents had only one telephone in the hall, and the whole family shared it.","t":"我祖父母家只有一支電話放在走廊,而全家人共用它。"},{"w":"phonograph","p":"n.","d":"an early machine for recording and playing sound","c":"留聲機(早期)","s":"Edison recorded his own voice on the phonograph, and people could hardly believe a machine could talk.","t":"愛迪生用留聲機錄下自己的聲音,而人們幾乎不敢相信機器會說話。"},{"w":"gramophone","p":"n.","d":"an old machine that plays music from flat discs","c":"唱機;留聲機","s":"My grandfather still plays old records on his gramophone, and the music sounds warm and a little scratchy.","t":"我祖父仍用他的唱機播放老唱片,而音樂聽起來溫暖又帶點沙沙聲。"},{"w":"camera","p":"n.","d":"a device for taking photographs","c":"相機","s":"I left my camera at home on our trip, but luckily my phone took clear pictures.","t":"旅行時我把相機留在家裡了,但幸好我的手機拍得很清楚。"},{"w":"photograph","p":"n.","d":"a picture made with a camera","c":"照片","s":"We found an old photograph of our town from 1900, and the main street looked completely different.","t":"我們找到一張1900年我們小鎮的老照片,而主要街道看起來完全不一樣。"},{"w":"light bulb","p":"n.","d":"a glass object that gives light when electricity passes through","c":"燈泡","s":"The light bulb in my room burned out, so I did my homework in the kitchen last night.","t":"我房間的燈泡燒壞了,所以我昨晚在廚房寫功課。"},{"w":"filament","p":"n.","d":"a very thin wire inside a light bulb that glows","c":"燈絲","s":"Edison tested thousands of materials for the filament, and he finally found one that glowed for hours.","t":"愛迪生為燈絲測試了上千種材料,而他終於找到一種能發光好幾個小時的。"},{"w":"printing press","p":"n.","d":"a machine for printing books and newspapers","c":"印刷機","s":"The printing press made books cheaper, so more people learned to read and share ideas.","t":"印刷機讓書變得更便宜,所以更多人學會閱讀和分享想法。"},{"w":"typewriter","p":"n.","d":"a machine with keys for printing letters onto paper","c":"打字機","s":"My mother learned to type on a typewriter, so she still presses the keys very hard on her laptop.","t":"我媽媽是用打字機學打字的,所以她在筆電上還是很用力地按鍵。"},{"w":"radio","p":"n.","d":"a device that receives sound broadcasts","c":"收音機;廣播","s":"We listen to the radio in the car every morning, and my dad always checks the traffic news.","t":"我們每天早上在車上聽廣播,而我爸總是會注意交通新聞。"},{"w":"transmitter","p":"n.","d":"equipment that sends out radio or TV signals","c":"發射器;發報機","s":"The station built a tall transmitter on the mountain, so people far away could hear the programmes.","t":"電台在山上蓋了一座高高的發射器,讓遠方的人也能收聽節目。"},{"w":"receiver","p":"n.","d":"the part of a telephone you hold to your ear","c":"聽筒;接收器","s":"She picked up the receiver and heard a strange voice, but the caller hung up before she could answer.","t":"她拿起聽筒聽到一個陌生的聲音,但對方在她回答前就掛斷了。"},{"w":"signal","p":"n.","d":"a sound, light or wave that carries information","c":"訊號;信號","s":"The guard waved a green flag as a signal, and the train slowly pulled out of the station.","t":"列車長揮動綠旗作為信號,而火車慢慢駛出車站。"},{"w":"refrigerator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that keeps food cold","c":"冰箱","s":"Before the refrigerator was invented, people kept food in cool cellars, but it still went bad quickly.","t":"在冰箱發明之前,人們把食物放在陰涼的地窖裡,但它還是很快就壞了。"},{"w":"canned food","p":"n.","d":"food kept in sealed metal containers","c":"罐頭食品","s":"Sailors took canned food on long voyages, because it stayed safe to eat for months.","t":"水手們長途航行時會帶罐頭食品,因為它可以安全食用好幾個月。"},{"w":"tin can","p":"n.","d":"a metal container for keeping food","c":"鐵罐;罐頭","s":"We made a simple phone from two tin can and a string, and it actually worked across the garden.","t":"我們用兩個鐵罐和一條繩子做了一支簡單的電話,而它真的能隔著花園通話。"},{"w":"tennis racket","p":"n.","d":"a bat with strings used to hit a tennis ball","c":"網球拍","s":"My new tennis racket is much lighter than my old wooden one, so I can swing it faster.","t":"我的新網球拍比舊的木頭球拍輕多了,所以我可以揮得更快。"},{"w":"graphite","p":"n.","d":"a soft black form of carbon used in pencils and sports equipment","c":"石墨","s":"Pencils contain graphite, not lead, and it is also used to make strong but light rackets.","t":"鉛筆含有的是石墨而不是鉛,而它也被用來做堅固又輕巧的球拍。"},{"w":"carbon fibre","p":"n.","d":"a very strong light material made from thin threads of carbon","c":"碳纖維","s":"Racing bikes are made of carbon fibre, so they are light but still very strong.","t":"競賽用腳踏車是用碳纖維做的,所以它們很輕卻依然非常堅固。"},{"w":"elevator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that carries people up and down in a building","c":"電梯","s":"The elevator made tall buildings possible, because nobody wanted to climb twenty floors every day.","t":"電梯讓高樓成為可能,因為沒有人想每天爬二十層樓。"},{"w":"escalator","p":"n.","d":"moving stairs","c":"手扶梯","s":"The escalator at the station was broken, so we carried our heavy suitcases up the stairs.","t":"車站的手扶梯壞了,所以我們把沉重的行李箱扛上樓梯。"},{"w":"stethoscope","p":"n.","d":"a tool doctors use to listen to your heart and breathing","c":"聽診器","s":"The doctor put the cold stethoscope on my chest, and she asked me to breathe in deeply.","t":"醫生把冰涼的聽診器放在我胸口,而她要我深呼吸。"},{"w":"vaccine","p":"n.","d":"a substance that protects people from a disease","c":"疫苗","s":"Edward Jenner made the first vaccine in 1796, and it protected millions of people from deadly smallpox.","t":"愛德華·詹納在1796年製成了第一支疫苗,而它保護了數百萬人免於致命的天花。"},{"w":"anaesthetic","p":"n.","d":"a drug that stops you feeling pain during an operation","c":"麻醉劑","s":"Before anaesthetic was used, operations were terribly painful, so surgeons had to work very fast.","t":"在使用麻醉劑之前,手術極度痛苦,所以外科醫生必須動作非常快。"},{"w":"penicillin","p":"n.","d":"a medicine that kills bacteria","c":"盤尼西林;青黴素","s":"Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin by accident, and it has saved millions of lives since then.","t":"亞歷山大·弗萊明意外發現了盤尼西林,而它從那時起已拯救了數百萬條生命。"},{"w":"plumbing","p":"n.","d":"the pipes that carry water in a building","c":"水管系統","s":"Modern plumbing brought clean water into homes, so people no longer had to carry buckets from the well.","t":"現代的水管系統把乾淨的水引進家中,所以人們不再需要從井裡提水。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (achieve – chemical)","cards":[{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in doing something after effort","c":"達成;實現","s":"Edison failed many times, but he finally achieve his goal of making a light bulb that lasted for hours.","t":"愛迪生失敗了很多次,但他最終實現了做出能亮好幾個小時燈泡的目標。"},{"w":"administration","p":"n.","d":"the work of organising and running a business or government","c":"行政;管理","s":"The factory needed more office staff for administration, because it now had thousands of workers to pay.","t":"工廠需要更多辦公室人員負責行政,因為它現在有數千名工人要發薪水。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help or support","c":"協助;幫助","s":"The old inventor needed assistance to finish his last machine, so his daughter helped him every evening.","t":"年老的發明家需要協助來完成他的最後一台機器,所以他女兒每天晚上都幫他。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of things that share the same features","c":"類別;種類","s":"The museum puts each invention into a category, such as transport or communication, so visitors can find them easily.","t":"博物館把每項發明歸入一個類別,例如交通或通訊,讓參觀者容易找到。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"the people who live in one area","c":"社區;群體","s":"When the mine closed, the whole community suffered, and many shops on the main street shut down.","t":"當礦坑關閉時,整個社區都受到影響,而大街上許多商店都關門了。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the art, ideas and customs of a society","c":"文化的","s":"Railways brought big cultural changes, because people from different regions began to meet and share ideas.","t":"鐵路帶來了巨大的文化變遷,因為來自不同地區的人們開始相遇並交流想法。"},{"w":"institute","p":"n.","d":"an organisation for research or education","c":"研究所;學會","s":"She joined a research institute after university, and now she studies how batteries can store more energy.","t":"她大學畢業後加入了一個研究機構,而現在她研究電池如何儲存更多能量。"},{"w":"journal","p":"n.","d":"a serious magazine about a subject, often science","c":"期刊","s":"The scientist published his results in a famous journal, and other researchers soon tested his ideas.","t":"那位科學家把研究結果發表在一份著名的期刊上,而其他研究者很快就測試了他的想法。"},{"w":"select","p":"v.","d":"to choose carefully from a group","c":"挑選;選擇","s":"The judges will select the three best student inventions, and the winners will travel to the national fair.","t":"評審將挑選出三件最佳學生發明,而得獎者將前往參加全國展覽會。"},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write to give an opinion","c":"評論;意見","s":"My teacher wrote a helpful comment on my report, so I added more facts about the steam engine.","t":"老師在我的報告上寫了一則有幫助的評語,所以我加入了更多關於蒸汽機的事實。"},{"w":"philosophy","p":"n.","d":"a set of beliefs about how to live or work","c":"理念;哲學","s":"The company's philosophy is to make simple products, and that is why its phones have so few buttons.","t":"這家公司的理念是製造簡單的產品,而這就是為什麼它的手機按鍵這麼少。"},{"w":"technology","p":"n.","d":"scientific knowledge used in practical ways","c":"科技;技術","s":"New technology changes how we work, but older people sometimes find it hard to keep up.","t":"新科技改變了我們工作的方式,但年長者有時覺得很難跟上。"},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"the chance or right to use something","c":"使用權;取得機會","s":"Poor families had no access to clean water, so they often became sick from dirty wells.","t":"貧窮家庭無法取得乾淨的水,所以他們常因骯髒的井水而生病。"},{"w":"civil","p":"adj.","d":"connected with ordinary citizens or the government, not the army","c":"公民的;民用的;土木(工程)的","s":"The bridge was built by civil engineers, and it still carries heavy traffic after a hundred years.","t":"那座橋是由土木工程師建造的,而它在一百年後仍承載著繁忙的交通。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information with others","c":"溝通;傳達","s":"The telegraph helped people communicate across countries, so business decisions could be made much faster.","t":"電報幫助人們跨國溝通,所以商業決策能做得快很多。"},{"w":"groundwork","p":"n.","d":"early work that makes later progress possible","c":"基礎;準備工作","s":"Early scientists laid the groundwork for modern electricity, so later inventors could build on their ideas.","t":"早期的科學家為現代電力打下了基礎,所以後來的發明家能在他們的想法上繼續發展。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要;總結","s":"Please write a summary of the chapter in five sentences, and include the most important inventions.","t":"請用五個句子寫出這一章的摘要,並且包含最重要的發明。"},{"w":"academy","p":"n.","d":"a school or society for special training or study","c":"學院;研究院","s":"The Royal academy of Sciences gave him a medal, and his invention became famous across Europe.","t":"皇家科學院頒給他一枚獎章,而他的發明因此聞名全歐洲。"},{"w":"energy","p":"n.","d":"power from sources like coal, oil or electricity","c":"能源","s":"Coal was the main source of energy in the 1800s, but today we are trying to use cleaner sources.","t":"煤是1800年代主要的能源來源,但今天我們正嘗試使用更乾淨的來源。"},{"w":"liberal","p":"adj.","d":"supporting freedom and gradual social change","c":"自由主義的;開明的","s":"The liberal politicians wanted to improve working conditions, but the factory owners fought against them.","t":"開明派政治人物想改善勞動條件,但工廠老闆們反對他們。"},{"w":"estate","p":"n.","d":"a large area of land with a big house, owned by one person","c":"莊園;地產","s":"The rich family owned a huge country estate, and they rarely visited the dirty factory towns.","t":"那個富有的家族擁有一座巨大的鄉間莊園,而他們很少造訪髒亂的工廠城鎮。"},{"w":"expert","p":"n.","d":"a person with special knowledge or skill","c":"專家","s":"We asked an expert to look at the old clock, and she said it was made in London in 1820.","t":"我們請一位專家看看這座老鐘,而她說它是1820年在倫敦製造的。"},{"w":"ministry","p":"n.","d":"a government department","c":"(政府)部會","s":"The ministry of Transport plans to build a new railway line, but local farmers are against it.","t":"交通部計劃興建一條新鐵路線,但當地農民反對。"},{"w":"aid","p":"n.","d":"help, especially money or food given to people in need","c":"援助;救助","s":"The charity sent food aid to the miners' families, because the men had been on strike for weeks.","t":"慈善團體送了食物援助給礦工家庭,因為那些男人已經罷工好幾週了。"},{"w":"chemical","p":"n.","d":"a substance made by or used in chemistry","c":"化學物質;化學品","s":"The factory poured a dangerous chemical into the river, and many fish died within a few days.","t":"工廠把一種危險的化學物質倒進河裡,而許多魚在幾天內就死了。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (classic – resourceful)","cards":[{"w":"classic","p":"adj.","d":"very good and a typical example of its kind","c":"經典的","s":"The Model T is a classic car, and collectors still pay a lot of money for one in good condition.","t":"T型車是一款經典汽車,而收藏家仍願意花大錢買一輛車況良好的。"},{"w":"definite","p":"adj.","d":"clear and certain","c":"明確的;肯定的","s":"We do not have a definite date for the museum trip yet, but it will probably be in December.","t":"我們還沒有參觀博物館的確定日期,但它可能會在十二月。"},{"w":"publication","p":"n.","d":"the act of printing a book or article for the public","c":"出版;刊物","s":"After the publication of his book, Darwin became famous, but many people strongly disagreed with him.","t":"他的書出版之後,達爾文變得很有名,但許多人強烈反對他。"},{"w":"found","p":"v.","d":"to start an organisation or company","c":"創立;建立","s":"Henry Ford found his car company in 1903, and it grew into one of the largest in the world.","t":"亨利·福特在1903年創立了他的汽車公司,而它成長為世界上最大的公司之一。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a huge change in the way people live or work","c":"革命;重大變革","s":"The smartphone started a revolution in communication, and now most people carry the internet in their pocket.","t":"智慧型手機掀起了一場通訊革命,而現在大多數人口袋裡都帶著網路。"},{"w":"subordinate","p":"n.","d":"a person with a lower position at work","c":"下屬;部屬","s":"The manager blamed his subordinate for the mistake, but everyone knew he had made the decision himself.","t":"經理把錯誤怪到他的下屬身上,但大家都知道是他自己做的決定。"},{"w":"consist","p":"v.","d":"to be made of (with \"of\")","c":"由……組成","s":"A steam engine mainly consist of a boiler, a cylinder and a piston, but there are many smaller parts too.","t":"蒸汽機主要由鍋爐、汽缸和活塞組成,但也有許多較小的零件。"},{"w":"economy","p":"n.","d":"the system of money, trade and industry in a country","c":"經濟","s":"Britain's economy grew rapidly in the 1800s, and it became the richest country in the world.","t":"英國的經濟在1800年代快速成長,而它成為了世界上最富有的國家。"},{"w":"legal","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law","c":"合法的","s":"It was legal to employ young children in the early mills, but new laws later stopped this practice.","t":"在早期工廠雇用幼童是合法的,但後來新的法律禁止了這種做法。"},{"w":"role","p":"n.","d":"the job or purpose someone or something has","c":"角色;作用","s":"Women played an important role in the textile mills, although they were paid much less than men.","t":"女性在紡織廠中扮演重要的角色,雖然她們的薪水比男性少很多。"},{"w":"similar","p":"adj.","d":"almost the same","c":"相似的","s":"My design is similar to my friend's, but mine uses less material and is easier to build.","t":"我的設計和朋友的很相似,但我的用料較少而且比較容易製作。"},{"w":"period","p":"n.","d":"a length of time in history","c":"時期","s":"The Victorian period saw many great inventions, and the population of Britain doubled at the same time.","t":"維多利亞時期出現許多偉大的發明,而英國人口同時也增加了一倍。"},{"w":"positive","p":"adj.","d":"good or helpful","c":"正面的;積極的","s":"The railway had a positive effect on farmers, because they could now sell fresh food in distant cities.","t":"鐵路對農民產生了正面的影響,因為他們現在能把新鮮食物賣到遙遠的城市。"},{"w":"emergence","p":"n.","d":"the process of starting to exist or become known","c":"出現;興起","s":"The emergence of factories changed family life, since parents now worked away from home all day.","t":"工廠的興起改變了家庭生活,因為父母現在整天都離家工作。"},{"w":"adoption","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting to use something new","c":"採用","s":"The adoption of electric lights made streets safer at night, so more people went out after dark.","t":"電燈的採用讓夜晚的街道更安全,所以更多人在天黑後外出。"},{"w":"commercialise","p":"v.","d":"to make money from a product or idea by selling it","c":"使商業化","s":"Many scientists made discoveries, but they did not know how to commercialise them, so others got rich instead.","t":"許多科學家有了發現,但他們不知道如何將其商業化,所以反而是別人致富了。"},{"w":"prosperity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being rich and successful","c":"繁榮;興旺","s":"The new port brought prosperity to the town, and many families could finally afford better houses.","t":"新港口為這個小鎮帶來了繁榮,而許多家庭終於買得起更好的房子。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"producing a lot","c":"多產的;有生產力的","s":"Factories were much more productive than home workshops, so the price of cloth dropped sharply.","t":"工廠比家庭作坊更有生產力,所以布料價格大幅下降。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"making a lot of money","c":"有利可圖的;賺錢的","s":"Selling cheap cotton shirts was very profitable, so more and more mills opened in northern England.","t":"販賣便宜的棉襯衫非常賺錢,所以越來越多工廠在英格蘭北部開設。"},{"w":"mercantile","p":"adj.","d":"connected with trade and merchants","c":"商業的;貿易的","s":"Liverpool was a busy mercantile city, and ships from all over the world unloaded goods in its docks.","t":"利物浦是一座繁忙的商業城市,而來自世界各地的船隻在它的碼頭卸貨。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"money used to start or grow a business","c":"資本;資金","s":"He needed capital to build his first factory, so he borrowed money from his wealthy uncle.","t":"他需要資金來蓋他的第一間工廠,所以他向富有的叔叔借錢。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"buying and selling, especially on a large scale","c":"商業;貿易","s":"Canals and railways helped commerce grow, because goods could reach customers faster and more cheaply.","t":"運河和鐵路幫助商業成長,因為貨物能更快、更便宜地送達顧客手中。"},{"w":"enterprise","p":"n.","d":"a business or company","c":"企業;事業","s":"Her small enterprise began in her kitchen, but now it sells handmade soap all over the country.","t":"她的小企業從她的廚房起步,而現在它在全國各地販售手工肥皂。"},{"w":"industrious","p":"adj.","d":"working hard","c":"勤奮的","s":"The industrious young engineer worked late every night, and his boss soon gave him a bigger project.","t":"那位勤奮的年輕工程師每晚都工作到很晚,而老闆很快就交給他更大的專案。"},{"w":"resourceful","p":"adj.","d":"good at finding clever ways to solve problems","c":"足智多謀的;機智的","s":"The resourceful miners built a pump from old parts, so they could keep working after the flood.","t":"足智多謀的礦工們用舊零件做了一台抽水機,所以他們在淹水後還能繼續工作。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (visionary – appalling)","cards":[{"w":"visionary","p":"adj.","d":"having bold, original ideas about the future","c":"有遠見的","s":"The visionary engineer imagined trains under the city, and fifty years later London opened its first underground line.","t":"那位有遠見的工程師構想了城市底下的火車,而五十年後倫敦開通了第一條地下鐵路線。"},{"w":"transformative","p":"adj.","d":"causing a great change","c":"具變革性的","s":"Electricity was a transformative invention, because it changed how people worked, travelled and spent their evenings.","t":"電是一項具變革性的發明,因為它改變了人們工作、旅行和度過夜晚的方式。"},{"w":"far-reaching","p":"adj.","d":"having a big effect on many things","c":"影響深遠的","s":"The new law had far-reaching effects, since it limited working hours in every factory in the country.","t":"這項新法律產生了影響深遠的效果,因為它限制了全國每家工廠的工時。"},{"w":"momentous","p":"adj.","d":"very important, especially for the future","c":"極重要的;重大的","s":"The first flight in 1903 was a momentous event, but only a few people saw it with their own eyes.","t":"1903年的首次飛行是一個重大的事件,但只有少數人親眼目睹。"},{"w":"watershed","p":"n.","d":"an event that marks a very important change","c":"分水嶺;轉折點","s":"The year 1830 was a watershed for travel, because the first passenger railway between two cities opened.","t":"1830年是旅行的分水嶺,因為第一條連接兩座城市的客運鐵路開通了。"},{"w":"origin","p":"n.","d":"the place or point where something begins","c":"起源","s":"The origin of the word \"robot\" is a Czech play, but now people all over the world use it.","t":"\"robot\"這個字的起源是一齣捷克劇作,但現在全世界的人都在使用它。"},{"w":"fame","p":"n.","d":"the state of being known by many people","c":"名聲;名氣","s":"The inventor won fame and money, but he said his greatest joy was solving difficult problems.","t":"這位發明家贏得了名聲和財富,但他說他最大的喜悅是解決困難的問題。"},{"w":"reputation","p":"n.","d":"the opinion people have about someone or something","c":"聲譽;名聲","s":"The company has a good reputation for safety, so many parents trust its car seats for their babies.","t":"這家公司在安全方面有良好的聲譽,所以許多父母信任它為嬰兒做的汽車座椅。"},{"w":"perfect","p":"v.","d":"to make something as good as possible","c":"使完美;改進到完善","s":"The Wright brothers spent years trying to perfect their flying machine, and they tested it hundreds of times.","t":"萊特兄弟花了好幾年試圖完善他們的飛行器,而他們測試了好幾百次。"},{"w":"multiply","p":"v.","d":"to increase greatly in number","c":"成倍增加","s":"The number of factories began to multiply quickly, and soon the sky over the city was full of smoke.","t":"工廠的數量開始迅速成倍增加,而很快城市上空就佈滿了煙霧。"},{"w":"diversify","p":"v.","d":"to start making a wider range of products","c":"使多樣化;多角化經營","s":"The company decided to diversify when cotton prices fell, so it also began making wool and silk.","t":"當棉花價格下跌時,這家公司決定多角化經營,所以它也開始生產羊毛和絲綢。"},{"w":"operate","p":"v.","d":"to make a machine work","c":"操作;運轉","s":"Only trained workers could operate the huge machines, but small children often cleaned underneath them while they ran.","t":"只有受過訓練的工人能操作這些巨大的機器,但小孩子們常在機器運轉時鑽到下方打掃。"},{"w":"spread","p":"v.","d":"to move or reach a larger area","c":"擴散;傳播","s":"News of the invention spread quickly, and soon factories in America were copying the British machines.","t":"這項發明的消息迅速傳開,而很快美國的工廠就仿造起英國的機器。"},{"w":"circulate","p":"v.","d":"to move or pass around","c":"流通;傳閱","s":"Newspapers began to circulate widely in the cities, so ordinary workers learned about politics and new ideas.","t":"報紙開始在城市中廣泛流通,所以一般工人得以了解政治和新思想。"},{"w":"supply","p":"n.","d":"an amount of something that is available to use","c":"供應;供給","s":"The city needed a steady supply of coal, so trains brought it in from the mines every day.","t":"城市需要穩定的煤供應,所以火車每天從礦場把煤運進來。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n.","d":"the need or wish of people to buy something","c":"需求","s":"demand for cheap clothes grew quickly, so mill owners bought more machines and hired more workers.","t":"對便宜衣服的需求迅速成長,所以工廠主購買了更多機器並雇用更多工人。"},{"w":"consume","p":"v.","d":"to use up fuel, energy or time","c":"消耗;耗費","s":"Early steam engines consume huge amounts of coal, but later designs were much more efficient.","t":"早期的蒸汽機消耗大量的煤,但後來的設計效率高得多。"},{"w":"economise","p":"v.","d":"to use less money or resources","c":"節約;節省","s":"My family tries to economise on electricity, so we turn off lights and unplug chargers every night.","t":"我家努力節約用電,所以我們每晚關燈並拔掉充電器。"},{"w":"inefficient","p":"adj.","d":"wasting time, energy or money","c":"效率低的","s":"The old machine was slow and inefficient, so the company replaced it with a modern one last year.","t":"那台舊機器又慢又沒效率,所以公司去年把它換成了新型的。"},{"w":"strenuous","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of physical effort","c":"費力的;艱苦的","s":"Mining was strenuous work, and most miners suffered from back pain before they turned forty.","t":"採礦是費力的工作,而大多數礦工在四十歲之前就飽受背痛之苦。"},{"w":"lethal","p":"adj.","d":"able to kill","c":"致命的","s":"Coal dust could be lethal in large amounts, but miners had no masks to protect their lungs.","t":"大量的煤塵可能是致命的,但礦工們沒有口罩來保護他們的肺。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing death","c":"致命的;導致死亡的","s":"There was a fatal accident at the factory last year, and it led to new safety rules for every machine.","t":"去年工廠發生了一起致命意外,而它促使每台機器都有了新的安全規定。"},{"w":"harmful","p":"adj.","d":"causing damage or injury","c":"有害的","s":"Smoke from the factories was harmful to people's health, but many families could not afford to move away.","t":"工廠排出的煙對人們的健康有害,但許多家庭沒有能力搬走。"},{"w":"squalid","p":"adj.","d":"very dirty and unpleasant because of poverty","c":"骯髒破敗的","s":"Many workers lived in squalid rooms without water, and their children often became sick in winter.","t":"許多工人住在沒有水的骯髒破敗的房間裡,而他們的孩子在冬天常常生病。"},{"w":"appalling","p":"adj.","d":"shockingly bad","c":"駭人的;極糟的","s":"The conditions in the mines were appalling, so reporters wrote angry articles about them in the newspapers.","t":"礦坑裡的環境極其惡劣,所以記者們在報紙上寫了憤怒的文章。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (deplorable – congestion)","cards":[{"w":"deplorable","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and deserving strong criticism","c":"可悲的;應受譴責的","s":"Charles Dickens described the deplorable life of poor children, and his novels made readers want change.","t":"查爾斯·狄更斯描寫了窮苦孩子悲慘的生活,而他的小說讓讀者渴望改變。"},{"w":"grim","p":"adj.","d":"unpleasant and depressing","c":"嚴酷的;陰沉的","s":"Factory towns looked grim and grey, but people still found ways to enjoy music and football.","t":"工廠城鎮看起來陰沉又灰暗,但人們仍然找到方法享受音樂和足球。"},{"w":"harsh","p":"adj.","d":"cruel, severe or unkind","c":"嚴苛的;殘酷的","s":"The rules in the mill were very harsh, and workers lost a day's pay if they arrived five minutes late.","t":"工廠裡的規定非常嚴苛,而工人遲到五分鐘就會被扣一天的工資。"},{"w":"destitute","p":"adj.","d":"having no money, food or home","c":"赤貧的;一無所有的","s":"When her husband died in the mine, the widow was left destitute, so she had to beg on the streets.","t":"當她丈夫死在礦坑中時,這位寡婦變得一貧如洗,所以她只好上街乞討。"},{"w":"marginalised","p":"adj.","d":"treated as unimportant and kept out of power","c":"被邊緣化的","s":"marginalised groups had no vote in the 1800s, so their problems were often ignored by the government.","t":"被邊緣化的群體在1800年代沒有投票權,所以他們的問題常被政府忽視。"},{"w":"unjust","p":"adj.","d":"not fair or morally right","c":"不公正的","s":"Workers felt the new rules were unjust, because owners became richer while their pay went down.","t":"工人們覺得新規定很不公正,因為老闆們越來越富有,而他們的薪水卻減少了。"},{"w":"injustice","p":"n.","d":"a situation that is unfair","c":"不公義;不公平","s":"The writer was angry about the injustice she saw in the mills, and she spent her life fighting for workers.","t":"那位作家對她在工廠裡看到的不公義感到憤怒,而她一生都在為工人奮鬥。"},{"w":"grievance","p":"n.","d":"a reason to complain about unfair treatment","c":"不滿;怨言","s":"The workers listed every grievance in a letter, and they sent it to the factory owner and the newspaper.","t":"工人們把每一項不滿列在一封信裡,並把它寄給工廠老闆和報社。"},{"w":"discontent","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being unhappy with a situation","c":"不滿;不平","s":"discontent grew among the weavers as machines took their jobs, and some of them broke the new looms.","t":"隨著機器奪走工作,織工之間的不滿日益增加,而他們之中有些人砸毀了新織布機。"},{"w":"rebel","p":"v.","d":"to fight against people in power","c":"反抗;造反","s":"The workers decided to rebel against the long hours, so they refused to enter the factory one morning.","t":"工人們決定反抗過長的工時,所以某天早上他們拒絕進入工廠。"},{"w":"rebellion","p":"n.","d":"an organised fight against people in power","c":"叛亂;反抗","s":"The army quickly stopped the rebellion, but the government later agreed to some of the workers' demands.","t":"軍隊迅速平定了這場反抗,但政府後來同意了工人們的部分要求。"},{"w":"militant","p":"adj.","d":"ready to use strong or violent action for a cause","c":"好戰的;激進的","s":"Some militant workers wanted to destroy the new machines, while others preferred a peaceful protest in the town square.","t":"有些激進的工人想摧毀新機器,而其他人比較偏好在鎮上廣場和平抗議。"},{"w":"statute","p":"n.","d":"a written law made by a government","c":"法令;法規","s":"A new statute banned children under nine from working in mills, and inspectors checked that owners obeyed.","t":"一項新法令禁止九歲以下兒童在工廠工作,而督察員檢查老闆們是否遵守。"},{"w":"outlaw","p":"v.","d":"to make something illegal","c":"宣布……為非法;禁止","s":"The government decided to outlaw the use of young boys as chimney sweeps, but the practice continued for years.","t":"政府決定立法禁止雇用小男孩掃煙囪,但這種做法仍持續了好幾年。"},{"w":"suffrage","p":"n.","d":"the right to vote in elections","c":"選舉權;投票權","s":"Workers fought for suffrage for many years, and finally most men in Britain could vote by 1884.","t":"工人們為爭取選舉權奮鬥了許多年,而到了1884年英國大多數男性終於可以投票。"},{"w":"modernise","p":"v.","d":"to make something more up to date","c":"使現代化","s":"The town plans to modernise its old train station, so it will have lifts and new waiting rooms next year.","t":"小鎮計劃將老舊的火車站現代化,所以明年它會有電梯和新的候車室。"},{"w":"populous","p":"adj.","d":"having a large population","c":"人口稠密的","s":"Manchester became a populous city very quickly, but its streets and houses were not ready for so many people.","t":"曼徹斯特很快就成為一座人口稠密的城市,但它的街道和房屋還沒準備好容納這麼多人。"},{"w":"metropolitan","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a large city","c":"大都會的","s":"The metropolitan railway carried thousands of workers every day, so the city could spread far into the countryside.","t":"大都會鐵路每天載運數千名工人,所以城市得以向鄉間遠遠擴展。"},{"w":"municipal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a town or city government","c":"市政的;市立的","s":"The municipal council built public baths, and poor families could finally wash in clean hot water.","t":"市議會興建了公共澡堂,而貧窮家庭終於能用乾淨的熱水洗澡。"},{"w":"civic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a town and its citizens","c":"市民的;城市的","s":"The new town hall was a symbol of civic pride, and local factory owners paid for most of it.","t":"新市政廳是市民驕傲的象徵,而當地的工廠老闆們支付了大部分費用。"},{"w":"epidemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads to many people quickly","c":"流行病;疫情","s":"A typhoid epidemic hit the city in 1850, and doctors realised that dirty water was the cause.","t":"1850年一場傷寒疫情侵襲這座城市,而醫生們意識到骯髒的水是元兇。"},{"w":"contagious","p":"adj.","d":"spreading easily from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"The disease was highly contagious, so sick children had to stay at home and could not go to school.","t":"這種疾病具有高度傳染性,所以生病的孩子必須待在家而不能上學。"},{"w":"mortality","p":"n.","d":"the number of deaths in a group","c":"死亡率","s":"Child mortality was very high in factory towns, but it fell after clean water was introduced.","t":"工廠城鎮的兒童死亡率非常高,但在引進乾淨的水之後就下降了。"},{"w":"hygiene","p":"n.","d":"keeping yourself and places clean to stay healthy","c":"衛生","s":"Good hygiene prevents many diseases, so the nurse taught the children to wash their hands before meals.","t":"良好的衛生習慣能預防許多疾病,所以護理師教孩子們飯前要洗手。"},{"w":"congestion","p":"n.","d":"too much traffic in one place","c":"擁擠;壅塞","s":"There was terrible congestion in the city centre this morning, and I was twenty minutes late for school.","t":"今天早上市中心的交通嚴重壅塞,而我上學遲到了二十分鐘。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (noteworthy – biological)","cards":[{"w":"noteworthy","p":"adj.","d":"interesting or important enough to be noticed","c":"值得注意的","s":"It is noteworthy that many great inventors had little formal education, but they never stopped learning on their own.","t":"值得注意的是,許多偉大的發明家沒受過多少正規教育,但他們從未停止自學。"},{"w":"striking","p":"adj.","d":"very noticeable or unusual","c":"顯著的;引人注目的","s":"There is a striking difference between old and new phones, and young people cannot imagine life with a dial phone.","t":"舊手機和新手機之間有顯著的差異,而年輕人無法想像使用撥盤電話的生活。"},{"w":"state-of-the-art","p":"adj.","d":"using the newest and best technology","c":"最先進的","s":"The hospital bought state-of-the-art equipment last year, so doctors can now find problems much earlier.","t":"醫院去年購置了最先進的設備,所以醫生現在能更早發現問題。"},{"w":"advanced","p":"adj.","d":"modern and highly developed","c":"先進的","s":"Britain had the most advanced machines in 1850, but Germany and America soon caught up.","t":"英國在1850年擁有最先進的機器,但德國和美國很快就迎頭趕上。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having new and creative ideas","c":"富想像力的","s":"The students came up with imaginative designs for a bridge, and one group used only paper and glue.","t":"學生們想出了富有想像力的橋梁設計,而其中一組只用了紙和膠水。"},{"w":"theoretical","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas rather than practice","c":"理論上的","s":"His plan was only theoretical at first, but after ten years of work he built a machine that really worked.","t":"他的計畫起初只是理論上的,但經過十年的努力他造出了一台真正能運作的機器。"},{"w":"applied","p":"adj.","d":"used in practical ways rather than just studied","c":"應用的","s":"She studies applied science, so she spends more time building devices than reading old theories.","t":"她唸的是應用科學,所以她花更多時間製作裝置,而不是閱讀舊理論。"},{"w":"scientific","p":"adj.","d":"connected with science","c":"科學的","s":"Faraday's scientific work on electricity was brilliant, although he left school at the age of thirteen.","t":"法拉第在電學方面的科學研究非常傑出,雖然他十三歲就離開了學校。"},{"w":"technological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with technology","c":"科技的;技術的","s":"Every technological change creates new jobs, but it also makes some old skills less useful.","t":"每一次科技變革都創造新工作,但它也讓一些舊技能變得較不實用。"},{"w":"develop","p":"v.","d":"to create or improve something over time","c":"開發;發展","s":"Engineers develop a safer lamp for miners, and it saved thousands of lives in the following years.","t":"工程師們開發出一種給礦工用的更安全的燈,而它在隨後幾年拯救了數千條人命。"},{"w":"extend","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer or larger","c":"延伸;擴大","s":"The company plans to extend the railway line to the coast, so tourists can visit the beach more easily.","t":"公司計劃把鐵路線延伸到海岸,讓遊客能更方便地前往海灘。"},{"w":"by-product","p":"n.","d":"something extra produced while making something else","c":"副產品","s":"Coal gas was a by-product of making coke, and soon it was used to light streets across the city.","t":"煤氣是製造焦炭的副產品,而很快它就被用來點亮全城的街道。"},{"w":"side effect","p":"n.","d":"an extra and usually bad result of something","c":"副作用","s":"Pollution was a serious side effect of industry, but many factory owners simply ignored it.","t":"污染是工業一項嚴重的副作用,但許多工廠老闆根本不予理會。"},{"w":"downside","p":"n.","d":"a disadvantage","c":"缺點;壞處","s":"The downside of living near the station is the noise, but it is very convenient for getting to work.","t":"住在車站附近的缺點是噪音,但上班非常方便。"},{"w":"wealth","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of money or property","c":"財富","s":"Industry created great wealth for factory owners, while most workers stayed poor for many years.","t":"工業為工廠老闆創造了巨大的財富,而大多數工人多年來仍然貧窮。"},{"w":"trade","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods","c":"貿易","s":"trade between Britain and India grew quickly, and ships carried cotton and tea across the oceans.","t":"英國和印度之間的貿易迅速成長,而船隻載運棉花和茶葉橫越大洋。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to bring goods into a country from abroad","c":"進口","s":"Britain had to import most of its cotton, because the plant could not grow in its cold climate.","t":"英國必須進口大部分棉花,因為這種植物無法在它寒冷的氣候中生長。"},{"w":"tariff","p":"n.","d":"a tax on goods coming into a country","c":"關稅","s":"The government added a tariff on foreign steel, so local steel companies could compete more easily.","t":"政府對外國鋼鐵加徵關稅,好讓本地鋼鐵公司更容易競爭。"},{"w":"rate","p":"n.","d":"the speed or frequency of something","c":"速度;比率","s":"New railways were built at an amazing rate, and by 1850 most big towns had a station.","t":"新鐵路以驚人的速度興建,而到了1850年大多數大城鎮都有車站。"},{"w":"figure","p":"n.","d":"a number, especially in official information","c":"數字;數據","s":"The figure for car sales rose again this year, but more people are now choosing electric cars.","t":"今年汽車銷售的數字又上升了,但現在更多人選擇電動車。"},{"w":"quantity","p":"n.","d":"an amount or number of something","c":"數量","s":"Factories could make a huge quantity of nails every day, so building houses became cheaper.","t":"工廠每天能製造大量的釘子,所以蓋房子變得更便宜。"},{"w":"velocity","p":"n.","d":"the speed of something in a particular direction","c":"速度","s":"The train reached a velocity of 100 kilometres an hour, and passengers were both excited and afraid.","t":"火車達到每小時100公里的速度,而乘客們既興奮又害怕。"},{"w":"gravity","p":"n.","d":"the force that pulls things towards the earth","c":"重力;地心引力","s":"Newton wondered why apples always fall down, and his ideas about gravity changed science and engineering forever.","t":"牛頓好奇蘋果為什麼總是往下掉,而他關於重力的想法永遠改變了科學和工程。"},{"w":"kinetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with movement","c":"動力的;運動的","s":"The water wheel turned the kinetic energy of the river into power, so the mill could grind grain.","t":"水車把河流的動能轉化為動力,所以磨坊可以磨穀物。"},{"w":"biological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with living things","c":"生物的","s":"Pasteur studied biological processes like milk going sour, and his work made food much safer.","t":"巴斯德研究牛奶變酸這類生物過程,而他的研究讓食物安全許多。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (compound – leisure)","cards":[{"w":"compound","p":"n.","d":"a substance made of two or more elements","c":"化合物","s":"Water is a compound of hydrogen and oxygen, but each of these gases behaves very differently alone.","t":"水是氫和氧的化合物,但這兩種氣體單獨存在時的性質非常不同。"},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"the parts or substances that something is made of","c":"成分;組成","s":"Scientists studied the composition of the metal, and they found that a little carbon made it much stronger.","t":"科學家研究這種金屬的成分,而他們發現少量的碳讓它堅固許多。"},{"w":"fraction","p":"n.","d":"a small part of something","c":"一小部分","s":"The new machine used only a fraction of the coal, so the factory saved a lot of money every year.","t":"新機器只用了一小部分的煤,所以工廠每年省下很多錢。"},{"w":"proof","p":"n.","d":"facts that show something is true","c":"證據;證明","s":"The inventor needed proof that he had the idea first, so he showed the court his dated notebooks.","t":"發明家需要證據證明是他先有這個點子的,所以他向法庭出示了標有日期的筆記本。"},{"w":"counterargument","p":"n.","d":"an argument against another argument","c":"反論;反駁論點","s":"Write one counterargument in your essay, and then explain why you still believe your own view is stronger.","t":"在你的文章中寫出一個反駁論點,然後解釋為什麼你仍然認為自己的觀點比較有力。"},{"w":"simplicity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to understand or use","c":"簡單;簡潔","s":"The bicycle became popular because of its simplicity, and almost anyone could learn to ride it in a day.","t":"腳踏車因為它的簡單而受歡迎,而幾乎任何人都能在一天內學會騎。"},{"w":"covert","p":"adj.","d":"secret or hidden","c":"祕密的;隱蔽的","s":"Some companies used covert methods to copy foreign machines, while others paid for the right to use them.","t":"有些公司用祕密的手段仿造外國機器,而其他公司則付費取得使用權。"},{"w":"noticeable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or notice","c":"明顯的","s":"There was a noticeable drop in pollution after the factory closed, and people could see the stars again.","t":"工廠關閉後污染有了明顯的下降,而人們又能看見星星了。"},{"w":"measurable","p":"adj.","d":"large enough to be measured","c":"可衡量的;顯著的","s":"Street lights led to a measurable fall in crime, so other towns quickly installed them too.","t":"路燈帶來了可衡量的犯罪率下降,所以其他城鎮也很快裝設了路燈。"},{"w":"restructure","p":"v.","d":"to organise a company or system in a new way","c":"重組;改組","s":"The car company had to restructure after losing money, and several factories were closed or sold.","t":"這家汽車公司虧損後不得不重組,而好幾間工廠被關閉或出售。"},{"w":"reorganise","p":"v.","d":"to arrange something in a new way","c":"重新安排;改組","s":"Henry Ford decided to reorganise his factory around a moving line, so each worker did only one simple task.","t":"亨利·福特決定圍繞著移動生產線重新安排他的工廠,所以每位工人只做一項簡單的工作。"},{"w":"introduce","p":"v.","d":"to bring something into use for the first time","c":"引進;推出","s":"The city introduce electric trams in 1900, and people could travel across town for a few pennies.","t":"這座城市在1900年引進了電車,而人們只要幾便士就能橫越城鎮。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to start selling a new product","c":"推出;發行","s":"The company will launch its new electric bike next month, but the price has not been announced yet.","t":"這家公司下個月將推出新款電動腳踏車,但價格還沒有公布。"},{"w":"recession","p":"n.","d":"a period when the economy is doing badly","c":"經濟衰退","s":"Many factories closed during the recession, and thousands of workers had to look for new jobs.","t":"許多工廠在經濟衰退期間關閉,而數千名工人必須另找工作。"},{"w":"boom","p":"n.","d":"a period of fast economic growth","c":"繁榮期;熱潮","s":"There was a railway boom in the 1840s, and thousands of people invested their savings in new lines.","t":"1840年代出現了一股鐵路熱潮,而成千上萬的人把積蓄投資在新路線上。"},{"w":"slump","p":"n.","d":"a sudden fall in prices or business","c":"暴跌;不景氣","s":"After the slump in cotton prices, many mill owners lost everything, and their workers lost their jobs.","t":"棉花價格暴跌之後,許多工廠主失去了一切,而他們的工人也丟了工作。"},{"w":"downturn","p":"n.","d":"a fall in business or economic activity","c":"下滑;衰退","s":"The downturn in steel sales hit the town hard, so the council started training people for other work.","t":"鋼鐵銷售的下滑重創了這個小鎮,所以議會開始培訓人們從事其他工作。"},{"w":"inflation","p":"n.","d":"a general rise in prices","c":"通貨膨脹","s":"inflation has made food much more expensive this year, so my family buys fewer snacks now.","t":"通貨膨脹讓今年的食物貴了很多,所以我家現在比較少買零食。"},{"w":"benefactor","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives money to help others","c":"捐助者;恩人","s":"A rich benefactor paid for the town's first public library, and workers could borrow books for free.","t":"一位富有的捐助者出資興建了小鎮的第一座公共圖書館,而工人們可以免費借書。"},{"w":"philanthropist","p":"n.","d":"a rich person who gives money to help people","c":"慈善家","s":"Andrew Carnegie made a fortune from steel, but he became a philanthropist and gave most of it away.","t":"安德魯·卡內基靠鋼鐵賺了大錢,但他成為一位慈善家並把大部分財富捐了出去。"},{"w":"consumerism","p":"n.","d":"the idea that buying lots of goods is good","c":"消費主義","s":"Cheap factory goods led to consumerism, and today many people buy things they do not really need.","t":"便宜的工廠商品導致了消費主義,而今天許多人購買並非真正需要的東西。"},{"w":"conglomerate","p":"n.","d":"a large company made of many different businesses","c":"企業集團","s":"The conglomerate owns car factories, hotels and a bank, so its decisions affect millions of people.","t":"這家企業集團擁有汽車工廠、飯店和一家銀行,所以它的決策影響數百萬人。"},{"w":"dividend","p":"n.","d":"a share of a company's profit paid to its owners","c":"股利;股息","s":"The railway company paid a large dividend every year, so many middle-class families bought its shares.","t":"鐵路公司每年都發放豐厚的股利,所以許多中產階級家庭買了它的股票。"},{"w":"shareholder","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns part of a company","c":"股東","s":"Every shareholder can vote at the annual meeting, but the biggest owners usually make the decisions.","t":"每位股東都可以在年度大會上投票,但通常是最大的股東做決定。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"閒暇;休閒","s":"Workers had very little leisure in the 1800s, but later laws gave them Saturday afternoons off.","t":"1800年代的工人幾乎沒有閒暇時間,但後來的法律讓他們週六下午可以休息。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (recreation – humanitarian)","cards":[{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities done for fun when you are not working","c":"娛樂;消遣","s":"Cheap train tickets made seaside trips a popular form of recreation, and workers' families loved the beach.","t":"便宜的火車票讓海邊旅遊成為一種受歡迎的消遣,而勞工家庭很喜歡海灘。"},{"w":"luxury","p":"n.","d":"something expensive that you enjoy but do not need","c":"奢侈品","s":"A car was a luxury in 1910, but today most families in Taiwan own at least one scooter.","t":"在1910年汽車是奢侈品,但今天台灣大多數家庭至少擁有一台機車。"},{"w":"modernity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being modern","c":"現代性;現代化","s":"Tall glass towers became a symbol of modernity, while old wooden houses were slowly knocked down.","t":"高聳的玻璃大樓成為現代化的象徵,而老舊的木屋則慢慢被拆除。"},{"w":"unconventional","p":"adj.","d":"very different from the usual way","c":"不落俗套的;非傳統的","s":"Her unconventional design used bamboo instead of steel, but it was strong enough to carry a small car.","t":"她非傳統的設計用竹子取代鋼材,但它堅固到足以承載一輛小汽車。"},{"w":"trailblazer","p":"n.","d":"a person who is the first to do something new","c":"開拓者;先驅","s":"Ada Lovelace was a trailblazer in computing, because she wrote programs before modern computers even existed.","t":"愛達·勒芙蕾絲是電腦領域的開拓者,因為她在現代電腦存在之前就寫出了程式。"},{"w":"mastermind","p":"n.","d":"a very clever person who plans something complex","c":"策劃者;幕後主腦","s":"Brunel was the mastermind behind the Great Western Railway, and he also designed huge iron ships.","t":"布魯內爾是大西部鐵路背後的策劃者,而他也設計了巨大的鐵船。"},{"w":"brilliance","p":"n.","d":"great intelligence or skill","c":"才華;卓越","s":"Everyone admired the brilliance of her idea, but it took ten years before anyone would pay to build it.","t":"大家都欽佩她想法中的才華,但過了十年才有人願意出錢把它造出來。"},{"w":"observation","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching something carefully","c":"觀察","s":"Careful observation of boiling water gave him an idea, and he started to experiment with steam power.","t":"對沸水的仔細觀察給了他一個點子,而他開始實驗蒸汽動力。"},{"w":"measurement","p":"n.","d":"a size or amount found by measuring","c":"測量;尺寸","s":"Every part needed an exact measurement, or the machine would not fit together properly at the end.","t":"每個零件都需要精確的尺寸,否則機器最後就無法正確組裝。"},{"w":"intellectual property","p":"n.phr.","d":"ideas and inventions that legally belong to their creator","c":"智慧財產","s":"Companies protect their intellectual property with patents, so others cannot copy their inventions for free.","t":"公司用專利保護他們的智慧財產,讓別人無法免費抄襲他們的發明。"},{"w":"litigation","p":"n.","d":"the process of taking a case to court","c":"訴訟","s":"The two inventors were in litigation for years, and the lawyers earned more money than either of them.","t":"這兩位發明家打了好幾年的官司,而律師賺的錢比他們任何一方都多。"},{"w":"rightful","p":"adj.","d":"legally or morally correct","c":"合法的;應有的","s":"The court decided she was the rightful owner of the patent, so the company had to pay her.","t":"法院判定她是這項專利的合法擁有者,所以那家公司必須付錢給她。"},{"w":"overheads","p":"n.","d":"regular business costs such as rent and electricity","c":"經常性開支;營運費用","s":"The shop's overheads were too high, so the owner moved to a smaller place outside the city centre.","t":"這家店的營運費用太高,所以老闆搬到市中心外一個較小的地方。"},{"w":"retail","p":"n.","d":"the sale of goods to the public in shops","c":"零售","s":"My cousin works in retail, and she says weekends before Chinese New Year are the busiest time.","t":"我表姊在零售業工作,而她說農曆新年前的週末是最忙的時候。"},{"w":"merchandise","p":"n.","d":"goods that are bought and sold","c":"商品;貨品","s":"The new department store displayed its merchandise in large glass windows, and crowds stopped to look.","t":"新的百貨公司在大玻璃櫥窗中展示它的商品,而人群停下來觀看。"},{"w":"marketplace","p":"n.","d":"the world of buying and selling","c":"市場","s":"Cheap goods from factories filled the marketplace, so small craftsmen found it hard to make a living.","t":"工廠生產的便宜商品充斥市場,所以小手工業者很難維生。"},{"w":"rivalry","p":"n.","d":"competition between people or groups","c":"競爭;對抗","s":"The rivalry between Edison and Tesla was famous, and both men claimed their system was safer.","t":"愛迪生和特斯拉之間的競爭很有名,而兩人都宣稱自己的系統比較安全。"},{"w":"hegemony","p":"n.","d":"control by one powerful country or group over others","c":"霸權","s":"Britain held industrial hegemony for most of the 1800s, but by 1900 America produced more steel.","t":"英國在1800年代大部分時間握有工業霸權,但到了1900年美國生產的鋼鐵更多。"},{"w":"superpower","p":"n.","d":"an extremely powerful country","c":"超級強國","s":"After the war, the country became a superpower, and its factories made goods for the whole world.","t":"戰後這個國家成為超級強國,而它的工廠為全世界製造商品。"},{"w":"geopolitical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with how geography affects politics between countries","c":"地緣政治的","s":"Coal and oil had huge geopolitical importance, so countries fought to control the regions where they were found.","t":"煤和石油具有巨大的地緣政治重要性,所以各國爭奪控制出產它們的地區。"},{"w":"colony","p":"n.","d":"a country or area controlled by another country","c":"殖民地","s":"India was a British colony at that time, and much of its cotton was sent to factories in England.","t":"印度當時是英國的殖民地,而它的大部分棉花被送到英格蘭的工廠。"},{"w":"imperialism","p":"n.","d":"a system in which a powerful country controls others","c":"帝國主義","s":"Industry and imperialism grew together, because factories needed raw materials from other parts of the world.","t":"工業和帝國主義一起成長,因為工廠需要來自世界其他地方的原料。"},{"w":"emancipation","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving people freedom","c":"解放","s":"The emancipation of enslaved people was a huge step, but freed workers still faced unfair treatment for decades.","t":"被奴役者的解放是重大的一步,但獲得自由的勞工在數十年間仍遭受不公平對待。"},{"w":"liberation","p":"n.","d":"the act of freeing someone from control","c":"解放;解脫","s":"The washing machine meant a kind of liberation for women, since they no longer spent a whole day washing clothes.","t":"洗衣機對女性來說意味著一種解放,因為她們不再花一整天洗衣服。"},{"w":"humanitarian","p":"adj.","d":"connected with helping people who are suffering","c":"人道主義的","s":"The doctor did humanitarian work in the slums, and he treated poor patients without asking for money.","t":"那位醫生在貧民窟從事人道工作,而他免費為貧窮病人看病。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (virtue – magnate)","cards":[{"w":"virtue","p":"n.","d":"a good quality in a person's character","c":"美德","s":"Victorians saw hard work as a virtue, so they believed poor people should simply work harder.","t":"維多利亞時代的人視勤奮為一種美德,所以他們認為窮人只要更努力工作就好。"},{"w":"corruption","p":"n.","d":"dishonest behaviour by people in power","c":"貪腐;腐敗","s":"There was corruption in the railway company, because some managers secretly took money from builders.","t":"鐵路公司裡有貪腐問題,因為一些經理私下收取營造商的錢。"},{"w":"fraud","p":"n.","d":"the crime of tricking people to get money","c":"詐欺","s":"The banker was arrested for fraud, because he had sold shares in a railway that did not exist.","t":"那名銀行家因詐欺被捕,因為他賣了一條根本不存在的鐵路的股份。"},{"w":"lawful","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law","c":"合法的","s":"Workers wanted a lawful way to protest, so they asked the government to allow trade unions.","t":"工人們想要一個合法的抗議方式,所以他們要求政府允許成立工會。"},{"w":"illicit","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law or rules","c":"非法的;違禁的","s":"Some sailors ran an illicit trade in stolen goods, but the port police finally caught them.","t":"有些水手從事贓物的非法交易,但港口警察最終抓到了他們。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"physical harm to the body","c":"傷害;受傷","s":"A serious injury meant a worker could lose his job, and his family might have nothing to eat.","t":"嚴重的受傷意味著工人可能丟掉工作,而他的家人可能會沒東西吃。"},{"w":"mishap","p":"n.","d":"a small accident or bad luck","c":"小意外;不幸事故","s":"There was a mishap during the demonstration, because the machine caught fire, but nobody was hurt.","t":"示範過程中發生了一個小意外,因為機器起火了,但沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"a very sad event, often with death","c":"悲劇;慘劇","s":"The mine disaster was a terrible tragedy, and the town still holds a memorial every year.","t":"那場礦災是一場可怕的悲劇,而小鎮至今每年仍舉行追悼會。"},{"w":"leap","p":"n.","d":"a sudden big change or improvement","c":"躍進;飛躍","s":"The telephone was a great leap forward, because people could hear each other's voices across countries.","t":"電話是一大躍進,因為人們能跨國聽見彼此的聲音。"},{"w":"stride","p":"n.","d":"an important step forward in progress","c":"進展;大步","s":"Medicine made huge stride in the 1800s, and many common diseases could finally be prevented or cured.","t":"醫學在1800年代取得了巨大的進展,而許多常見疾病終於可以預防或治癒。"},{"w":"pattern","p":"n.","d":"a regular way in which something happens","c":"模式;規律","s":"Historians noticed a pattern in the strikes, because they usually happened when food prices went up.","t":"歷史學家注意到罷工中的一種規律,因為它們通常在糧價上漲時發生。"},{"w":"uptake","p":"n.","d":"the rate at which people start using something","c":"採用率;接受程度","s":"The uptake of electric cars has been slow in some areas, because there are not enough charging stations.","t":"在某些地區電動車的採用率一直很慢,因為充電站不夠多。"},{"w":"societal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with society","c":"社會的","s":"The car caused huge societal changes, since people could live far from work and still arrive on time.","t":"汽車引起了巨大的社會變化,因為人們可以住得離工作地點很遠又仍準時到達。"},{"w":"fiscal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with government money and taxes","c":"財政的","s":"The government had a fiscal problem after building so many railways, so it raised taxes on tobacco.","t":"政府興建了這麼多鐵路後出現財政問題,所以它提高了菸草稅。"},{"w":"monetary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money","c":"貨幣的;金錢的","s":"The inventor received no monetary reward for his idea, but he was proud that it helped so many people.","t":"發明家沒有因為他的點子得到任何金錢報酬,但他很自豪它幫助了那麼多人。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"connected with towns and cities","c":"城市的;都市的","s":"urban areas grew very quickly during the Industrial Revolution, but small villages lost many young people.","t":"都市地區在工業革命期間成長得非常快,但小村莊失去了許多年輕人。"},{"w":"suburban","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the areas around a city where people live","c":"郊區的","s":"The new railway created suburban towns, and office workers could live in quiet streets with gardens.","t":"新鐵路創造了郊區城鎮,而上班族可以住在有花園的安靜街道上。"},{"w":"mobility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move or travel easily","c":"流動性;移動能力","s":"Cars gave people much more mobility, so they could take jobs in other towns without moving house.","t":"汽車給了人們更多的移動能力,所以他們不必搬家就能在其他城鎮工作。"},{"w":"plentiful","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts","c":"充足的;豐富的","s":"Coal was plentiful in northern England, so many factories were built close to the mines to save money.","t":"英格蘭北部的煤很豐富,所以許多工廠都蓋在礦場附近以節省成本。"},{"w":"workable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used successfully","c":"可行的;可運作的","s":"His first plan was not workable, but after many changes the engine finally ran without stopping.","t":"他的第一個計畫並不可行,但經過多次修改後,引擎終於能不停地運轉。"},{"w":"inexhaustible","p":"adj.","d":"so large that it can never be used up","c":"取之不盡的","s":"People once thought coal was inexhaustible, but now we know that it will run out one day.","t":"人們曾經以為煤是取之不盡的,但現在我們知道它總有一天會用完。"},{"w":"wasteful","p":"adj.","d":"using more than is needed","c":"浪費的","s":"Old engines were very wasteful, because most of the heat escaped instead of moving the machine.","t":"舊引擎非常浪費,因為大部分的熱都散失了,而不是用來推動機器。"},{"w":"waste","p":"n.","d":"material that is thrown away after use","c":"廢棄物;垃圾","s":"Factories dumped their waste into nearby rivers, so the water turned black and smelled terrible in summer.","t":"工廠把廢棄物傾倒進附近的河裡,所以河水變黑,夏天時更是臭氣沖天。"},{"w":"tycoon","p":"n.","d":"a very rich and powerful businessperson","c":"大亨;巨頭","s":"The oil tycoon owned dozens of companies, but he started his career as a poor office clerk.","t":"那位石油大亨擁有數十家公司,但他的職業生涯是從一名貧窮的辦公室職員開始的。"},{"w":"magnate","p":"n.","d":"a rich and powerful person in a particular industry","c":"(某行業的)巨頭;大亨","s":"The railway magnate built a huge mansion, while the workers who laid his tracks lived in tents.","t":"那位鐵路巨頭蓋了一座巨大的豪宅,而為他鋪設鐵軌的工人卻住在帳篷裡。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"full steam ahead","p":"phr.","d":"moving forward with full energy and speed","c":"全速前進","s":"Once the bank gave us the loan, it was full steam ahead with the project, and we finished it in six months.","t":"銀行一借給我們貸款,這個計畫就全速前進,而我們在六個月內就完成了。"},{"w":"run out of steam","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose energy or enthusiasm","c":"失去動力;精疲力盡","s":"I started my essay with lots of ideas, but I run out of steam after the first page and had to take a break.","t":"我一開始寫文章時有很多點子,但寫完第一頁後我就失去動力,只好休息一下。"},{"w":"pick up steam","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become stronger, faster or more popular","c":"逐漸加速;勢頭增強","s":"The campaign for shorter working hours began slowly, but it pick up steam when newspapers reported on child workers.","t":"爭取縮短工時的運動起初進展緩慢,但在報紙報導童工之後就聲勢漸增。"},{"w":"reinvent the wheel","p":"v.phr.","d":"to waste time making something that already exists","c":"重複發明輪子;做白工","s":"We do not need to reinvent the wheel, because there is already a good app for planning group projects.","t":"我們不需要重複發明輪子,因為已經有一個很好的應用程式可以規劃小組作業。"},{"w":"necessity is the mother of invention","p":"phr.","d":"people invent things when they really need them","c":"需要為發明之母","s":"The campers had no pot, so they cooked rice in a bamboo tube, which shows that necessity is the mother of invention.","t":"露營的人沒有鍋子,所以他們用竹筒煮飯,這說明了需要為發明之母。"},{"w":"back to the drawing board","p":"phr.","d":"time to start planning again after a failure","c":"從頭再來;重新規劃","s":"Our paper bridge collapsed under the first book, so it was back to the drawing board for our team.","t":"我們的紙橋在放上第一本書時就垮了,所以我們這組只好從頭再來。"},{"w":"ahead of one's time","p":"adj.phr.","d":"having ideas too new for the people of that time","c":"超越時代的","s":"Da Vinci was ahead of one's time, because he drew helicopters and tanks hundreds of years before they were built.","t":"達文西是超越他那個時代的人,因為他在直升機和坦克被造出來的數百年前就畫出了它們。"},{"w":"turning point","p":"n.phr.","d":"a moment when a big change happens","c":"轉捩點","s":"Winning the science fair was a turning point in her life, and she decided to become an engineer.","t":"贏得科展是她人生的轉捩點,而她決定要成為一名工程師。"},{"w":"the daily grind","p":"n.phr.","d":"boring and tiring work that you do every day","c":"日復一日的苦差事","s":"Factory workers faced the daily grind of twelve-hour shifts, and they rarely had time to rest.","t":"工廠工人面對著每天十二小時輪班的日常苦差事,而他們很少有時間休息。"},{"w":"come up with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think of an idea or plan","c":"想出","s":"Our team had to come up with a way to clean the beach, and we designed a simple floating net.","t":"我們這組必須想出一個清理海灘的方法,而我們設計了一個簡單的浮動網子。"},{"w":"put into practice","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start using an idea or plan in real life","c":"付諸實行","s":"The school put into practice the new recycling plan last month, and the amount of rubbish has already dropped.","t":"學校上個月把新的回收計畫付諸實行,而垃圾量已經減少了。"},{"w":"in the pipeline","p":"adj.phr.","d":"being planned or developed and coming soon","c":"籌備中;即將推出","s":"A new train line to the airport is in the pipeline, but it will not open until 2030.","t":"一條通往機場的新鐵路線正在籌備中,但它要到2030年才會通車。"},{"w":"on the right track","p":"adj.phr.","d":"doing something in a way that will lead to success","c":"方向正確","s":"My teacher said my project was on the right track, so I just need to add more data.","t":"老師說我的專題方向正確,所以我只需要再加入更多數據。"},{"w":"go off the rails","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start behaving badly or failing","c":"出軌;失控","s":"The project began to go off the rails when the leader left, and nobody knew what to do next.","t":"領導者離開後這個計畫開始失控,而沒有人知道接下來該做什麼。"},{"w":"run like clockwork","p":"v.phr.","d":"to happen exactly as planned without problems","c":"運作順暢;井然有序","s":"The school sports day run like clockwork, because the teachers had planned every detail weeks before.","t":"學校運動會進行得井然有序,因為老師們好幾週前就規劃好了每個細節。"},{"w":"the best thing since sliced bread","p":"n.phr.","d":"an excellent new invention or idea (humorous)","c":"最棒的新發明","s":"My grandma thinks video calls are the best thing since sliced bread, because she can see her grandchildren every day.","t":"我奶奶覺得視訊通話是有史以來最棒的發明,因為她每天都能看到孫子們。"},{"w":"the brainchild of","p":"n.phr.","d":"an idea or invention created by a particular person","c":"……的心血結晶","s":"The underground railway was the brainchild of a lawyer named Charles Pearson, but he died before it opened.","t":"地下鐵路是一位名叫查爾斯·皮爾森的律師的心血結晶,但他在通車前就去世了。"},{"w":"make ends meet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have just enough money to live","c":"勉強維持生計","s":"Many families could not make ends meet on one wage, so the children also had to work in the mills.","t":"許多家庭靠一份工資無法維持生計,所以孩子們也必須到工廠工作。"},{"w":"think outside the box","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think in a new and creative way","c":"跳脫框架思考","s":"To solve the problem, we had to think outside the box, so we used old bottles to build a greenhouse.","t":"為了解決問題,我們必須跳脫框架思考,所以我們用舊瓶子蓋了一座溫室。"},{"w":"set the wheels in motion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start a process","c":"啟動;開始進行","s":"The mayor set the wheels in motion for a new bike lane, and work will start next spring.","t":"市長啟動了新自行車道的計畫,而工程將在明年春天開始。"}]}];
